tine eval_rows ( d , ks , jac , ok , only ) type ( eclipse_opt_data ), intent ( inout ) :: d real ( wp ), dimension (:), intent ( out ) :: ks real ( wp ), dimension (:), intent ( out ), optional :: jac logical , intent ( out ), optional :: ok !! false if a row couldn't be evaluated (see [[row_ks]]) logical , dimension (:), intent ( in ), optional :: only !! evaluate only these rows (the others' `ks` are 0, !! and their partials are not set) integer :: k , j , offset integer , dimension (:), allocatable :: first_nz !! index in `jac` of each row's first nonzero, minus 1 real ( wp ) :: t0 , tf , dt , h , fp , fm real ( wp ), dimension ( 6 ) :: x0r , xp real ( wp ) :: tp0 , tpf logical :: ok_k , all_ok allocate ( first_nz ( size ( d % rows ))) offset = 0 do k = 1 , size ( d % rows ) first_nz ( k ) = offset offset = offset + d % rows ( k )% ncol end do h = d % mission % eclipse_opt_fd_step all_ok = . true . !$OMP PARALLEL DO PRIVATE(k,j,t0,tf,dt,x0r,xp,tp0,tpf,fp,fm,ok_k) SCHEDULE(dynamic) do k = 1 , size ( d % rows ) if ( present ( only )) then if (. not . only ( k )) then ks ( k ) = zero cycle end if end if associate ( row => d % rows ( k ), seg => d % mission % segs ( d % rows ( k )% iseg )) t0 = seg % data % t0 tf = seg % data % tf x0r = seg % data % x0_rotating ks ( k ) = row_ks ( d % mission , seg , row , t0 , tf , x0r , ok_k ) if (. not . ok_k ) all_ok = . false . if ( present ( jac )) then do j = 1 , row % ncol dt = h * d % mission % xscale ( row % col ( j )) ! the unscaled change [days, km or km/s] call perturbed ( row , j , t0 , tf , x0r , + dt , tp0 , tpf , xp ) fp = row_ks ( d % mission , seg , row , tp0 , tpf , xp , ok_k ) if (. not . ok_k ) all_ok = . false . call perturbed ( row , j , t0 , tf , x0r , - dt , tp0 , tpf , xp ) fm = row_ks ( d % mission , seg , row , tp0 , tpf , xp , ok_k ) if (. not . ok_k ) all_ok = . false . jac ( first_nz ( k ) + j ) = ( fp - fm ) / ( 2.0_wp * h ) end do end if end associate end do !$OMP END PARALLEL DO if ( present ( ok )) ok = all_ok contains pure subroutine perturbed ( row , j , t0 , tf , x0r , delta , tp0 , tpf , xp ) !! the segment's inputs with variable `j` of the row changed by `delta` !! (everything is passed in: an internal procedure would see the host's !! variables, not the OpenMP thread's private copies) type ( eclipse_row ), intent ( in ) :: row integer , intent ( in ) :: j real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: t0 , tf , delta real ( wp ), dimension ( 6 ), intent ( in ) :: x0r real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: tp0 , tpf real ( wp ), dimension ( 6 ), intent ( out ) :: xp tp0 = t0 ; tpf = tf ; xp = x0r select case ( row % kind ( j )) case ( 0 ) tp0 = t0 + delta if ( row % tf_with_t0 ) tpf = tf + delta case ( 1 : 6 ) xp ( row % kind ( j )) = x0r ( row % kind ( j )) + delta end select end subroutine perturbed end subroutine eval_rows","tags":"","url":"proc/eval_rows.html"},{"title":"newton_finish – halo","text":"subroutine newton_finish(d, x) The Newton finish ( eclipse_opt_newton_finish ): from the optimization's point, solve\nhalo's continuity constraints and, as equalities , the\neclipse rows that are at or near their bound ( plus eclipse_opt_newton_active_tol ), with halo's minimum-norm Newton solver (nlesolver, with\nhalo's sparse linear solver). The optimization's point is near feasible but its\ncontinuity isn't converged; a solve of the continuity alone ( eclipse_opt_polish ) moves\nthe trajectory back into the shadow, but with the active rows held at their bound it\ncan't. A row left free that falls below its bound is added to the equalities, and the\nsolve repeated (from where it ended). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( eclipse_opt_data ), intent(inout), target :: d real(kind=wp), intent(inout), dimension(:) :: x the optimization's point (halo's scaled variables); replaced by the solution Calls proc~~newton_finish~~CallsGraph proc~newton_finish newton_finish destroy destroy proc~newton_finish->destroy initialize initialize proc~newton_finish->initialize kt 