!! the functions integer , intent ( in ) :: iter !! the iteration integer :: m select type ( me ) type is ( eclipse_newton_type ) m = me % d % m_halo if ( size ( f ) > m ) then write ( * , '(A,I4,A,ES12.4,A,ES12.4)' ) '     iter ' , iter , ': continuity norm ' , norm2 ( f ( 1 : m )), & ', eclipse rows max |KS - phi_min| ' , maxval ( abs ( f ( m + 1 :))) else write ( * , '(A,I4,A,ES12.4)' ) '     iter ' , iter , ': continuity norm ' , norm2 ( f ( 1 : m )) end if class default error stop 'newton_export: invalid class' end select end subroutine newton_export","tags":"","url":"proc/newton_export.html"},{"title":"equilibrate – halo","text":"subroutine equilibrate(d, x) Equilibrate the continuity Jacobian at x for the optimization ( eclipse_opt_equilibrate ):\nalternately normalize its rows (weights w ) and its columns (the variables' factors r ,\nthe optimization's variables being x/r ), a few times, so that the rows and the columns\nall have 2-norms near 1. This lowers the condition number of the KKT systems of sqpopt's\nQP subproblems (for 100 revolutions, J's condition number goes from 8e4 to 7e2). The\nobjective, |x/r - x0/r|&#94;2/2 , is then measured in these units. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( eclipse_opt_data ), intent(inout) :: d real(kind=wp), intent(in), dimension(:) :: x Calls proc~~equilibrate~~CallsGraph proc~equilibrate equilibrate proc~compute_jacobian_stm mission_type%compute_jacobian_stm proc~equilibrate->proc~compute_jacobian_stm proc~define_problem_size mission_type%define_problem_size proc~compute_jacobian_stm->proc~define_problem_size proc~earth_moon_frame_matrices earth_moon_frame_matrices proc~compute_jacobian_stm->proc~earth_moon_frame_matrices proc~get_sparsity_pattern mission_type%get_sparsity_pattern proc~compute_jacobian_stm->proc~get_sparsity_pattern proc~propagate_segment_stm segment%propagate_segment_stm proc~compute_jacobian_stm->proc~propagate_segment_stm proc~put_x_in_segments mission_type%put_x_in_segments proc~