rated variables type ( icrf_frame ) :: inertial type ( two_body_rotating_frame ) :: rotating real ( wp ) :: etf real ( wp ), dimension ( 6 ) :: xf !! inertial - from the propagation real ( wp ), dimension ( 6 ) :: xf_rotating logical :: status_ok integer :: integration_mode if ( present ( mode )) then integration_mode = mode else integration_mode = 1 end if ! integrate in local time (from 0 at t0), see t_offset: me % t_offset = me % data % t0 * day2sec t = zero tf = ( me % data % tf - me % data % t0 ) * day2sec neq = merge ( n_eoms_stm , n_eoms , me % stm_mode ) x = zero x ( 1 : n_eoms ) = me % data % x0 ! inertial state if ( me % stm_mode ) x ( n_eoms + 1 : neq ) = identity_stm () ! (not integrated here: its derivatives are zero) !write(*,*) '' !write(*,*) 'propagate segment '//me%name, t0, tf !write(*,*) 't0:',t0 !write(*,'(A,*(F15.3,1X))') 'x0:',x !write(*,*) 'tf:',tf me % compute_stm = . false . call me % first_call () !restarting the integration if ( present ( tstep )) then call me % integrate ( t , x ( 1 : neq ), tf , idid = idid , integration_mode = integration_mode , tstep = tstep ) else call me % integrate ( t , x ( 1 : neq ), tf , idid = idid , integration_mode = integration_mode ) end if me % t_offset = zero me % failed = . false . if ( idid < 0 ) then if ( me % soft_fail ) then me % failed = . true . return end if write ( * , '(A,*(I5/))' ) 'idid: ' , idid error stop 'error in integrator' end if xf = x ( 1 : n_eoms ) ! final state [inertial frame] ! also save the rotating frame state at tf (to compute the constraint violations): etf = me % data % et_ref + me % data % tf * day2sec ! convert to ephemeris time [sec] inertial = icrf_frame ( b = body_moon ) rotating = two_body_rotating_frame ( primary_body = body_earth ,& secondary_body = body_moon ,& center = center_at_secondary_body ,& et = etf ) ! from inertial to rotating: call inertial % transform ( xf , rotating , etf , me % eph , xf_rotating , status_ok ) if (. not . status_ok ) error stop 'transformation error in propagate_segment' ! put final states in the segment: call me % set_outputs ( xf , xf_rotating ) end subroutine propagate_segment","tags":"","url":"proc/propagate_segment.html"},{"title":"propagate_segment_stm – halo","text":"public  subroutine propagate_segment_stm(me) Propagate a segment with its state transition matrix, and compute the analytic\npartials of its final rotating-frame state (for jacobian_mode=2 ): dxf_dx0 : w.r.t. the initial rotating-frame state, dxf_dt0 : w.r.t. the\n  initial epoch (at fixed final epoch, and fixed rotating-frame initial state ), dxf_dtf : w.r.t. the final epoch, where is the inertial state transition matrix, the equations\nof motion, and , the inertial-to-rotating and rotating-to-inertial\ntransformations (see two_body_rotating_frame_matrices ). The epoch partial uses . The final state (and its rotating-frame version) is also set, as by propagate_segment . Type Bound segment Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( segment ), intent(inout) :: me Calls proc~~propagate_segment_stm~~CallsGraph proc~propagate_segment_stm segment%propagate_segment_stm first_call first_call proc~propagate_segment_stm->first_call icrf_frame icrf_frame proc~propagate_segment_stm->icrf_frame integrate integrate proc~propagate_segment_stm->integrate proc~ballistic_derivs ballistic_derivs proc~propagate_segment_stm->proc~ballistic_derivs proc~earth_moon_frame_matrices earth_moon_frame_matrices proc~propagate_segment_stm->proc~earth_moon_frame_matrices proc~identity_stm identity_stm proc~propagate_segment_stm->proc~identity_stm proc~set_segment_outputs segment%set_segment_outputs proc~propagate_segment_stm->proc~set_segment_outputs transform transform proc~propagate_segment_stm->transform two_body_rotating_frame two_body_rotating_frame proc~propagate_segment_stm->two_body_rotating_frame get_acc get_acc proc~ballistic_derivs->get_acc get_r get_r proc~ballistic_derivs->get_r icrf_to_iau_moon icrf_to_iau_moon proc~ballistic_derivs->icr