res in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Called by proc~~add_int~~CalledByGraph proc~add_int text_buffer%add_int proc~segment_trajectory_json segment_trajectory_json proc~segment_trajectory_json->proc~add_int proc~export_trajectory_json_file mission_type%export_trajectory_json_file proc~export_trajectory_json_file->proc~segment_trajectory_json proc~halo_solver_main halo_solver_main proc~halo_solver_main->proc~export_trajectory_json_file Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code pure subroutine add_int ( me , i ) class ( text_buffer ), intent ( inout ) :: me integer , intent ( in ) :: i call add_digits ( me , int ( i , int64 ), negative = i < 0 ) end subroutine add_int","tags":"","url":"proc/add_int.html"},{"title":"add_real – halo","text":"private pure subroutine add_real(me, x) Append a real number, in JSON syntax, in double precision (also when wp is\nquad precision: the trajectory files are for plotting and SPK files, which are\ndouble precision), with 17 significant digits\n(e.g., 8.2031911203980994E+8 ; trailing zeros are removed, e.g. 1.5E+0 ). The 17 digits are correctly rounded, so the number reads back as exactly the\nsame double precision value. |x| is scaled to a 17-digit integer by an exact\npower of ten ( ), and the rounding error of that product\n(or quotient) is computed exactly (Dekker's two-product), so the integer is the\ncorrectly rounded one. Numbers too small or too large for this\n(|x| < 1e-6 or |x| >= 1e39) are formatted with a write statement instead.\nNon-finite numbers are written as null , since JSON has no NaN or Infinity. Type Bound text_buffer Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( text_buffer ), intent(inout) :: me real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: x the number (converted to double precision, if wp is not) Calls proc~~add_real~~CallsGraph proc~add_real text_buffer%add_real proc~add_digits add_digits proc~add_real->proc~add_digits proc~add_str text_buffer%add_str proc~add_real->proc~add_str proc~reserve text_buffer%reserve proc~add_real->proc~reserve proc~scaled scaled proc~add_real->proc~scaled proc~add_digits->proc~add_str proc~add_str->proc~reserve proc~two_prod two_prod proc~scaled->proc~two_prod proc~split split proc~two_prod->proc~split Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Called by proc~~add_real~~CalledByGraph proc~add_real text_buffer%add_real proc~add_real_list text_buffer%add_real_list proc~add_real_list->proc~add_real proc~add_real_array text_buffer%add_real_array proc~add_real_array->proc~add_real_list proc~write_json_real_array write_json_real_array proc~write_json_real_array->proc~add_real_list proc~generate_eclipse_data mission_type%generate_eclipse_data proc~generate_eclipse_data->proc~write_json_real_array proc~segment_trajectory_json segment_trajectory_json proc~segment_trajectory_json->proc~add_real_array proc~export_trajectory_json_file mission_type%export_trajectory_json_file proc~export_trajectory_json_file->proc~segment_trajectory_json proc~halo_solver_main halo_solver_main proc~halo_solver_main->proc~generate_eclipse_data proc~halo_solver_main->proc~export_trajectory_json_file Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code pure subroutine add_real ( me , x ) class ( text_buffer ), intent ( inout ) :: me real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: x !! the number (converted to double precision, if `wp` is not) integer ( int64 ), parameter :: ten16 = 10000000000000000_int64 !! 10&#94;16 integer ( int64 ), parameter :: ten17 = 10_int64 * ten16 !! 10&#94;17 real ( dp ) :: xd , ax integer :: e10 , i , last integer ( int64 ) :: im logical :: ok character ( len = 17 ) :: digits character ( len = 30 ) :: str xd = real ( x , dp ) if (. not . ieee_is_finite ( xd )) then call me % add_str ( 'null' ) return end if if ( xd == 0.0_dp ) then call me % add_str ( '0.0' ) return end if ! im = |x| * 10&#94;(16-e10), rounded, should have 17 digits: ax = abs ( xd ) e10 = floor ( log10 ( ax )) call scaled ( ax , 16 - e10 , im , ok ) ! (log10 may be off by one near powers of ten) if ( ok . and . im >= ten17 ) then e10 = e10 + 1 call scaled ( ax , 16 - e10 , im , ok ) else if ( ok . and . im < ten16 ) then e10 = e10 - 1 call scaled ( ax , 16 - e10 , im , ok ) end if if ( ok . and . im == ten17 ) then ! rounded up to the next power of ten (e.g., 9.99999999999999999) im = ten16 e10 = e10 + 1 end if if (. not . ok ) then ! out of the range of the exact powers of ten: write ( str , '(ES24.16E3)' ) xd call me % add_str ( trim ( adjustl ( str ))) return end if ! the 17 digits: do i = 17 , 1 , - 1 digits ( i : i ) = achar ( iachar ( '0' ) + int ( mod ( im , 10_int64 ))) im = im / 10_int64 end do ! remove the trailing zeros (keeping at least one digit after the decimal point): last = 17 do while ( last > 2 . and . digits ( last : last ) == '0' ) last = last - 1 end do call me % reserve ( 30 ) if ( xd < 0.0_dp ) call me % add_str ( '-' ) call me % add_str ( digits ( 1 : 1 ) // '.' // digits ( 2 : last ) // 'E' ) if ( e10 >= 0 ) call me % add_str ( '+' ) call add_digits ( me , int ( e10 , int64 ), negative = e10 < 0 ) end subroutine add_real","tags":"","url":"proc/add_real.html"},{"title":"scaled – halo","text":"private pure subroutine scaled(a, k, im, ok) ( ), correctly rounded to an integer, when the\nresult is about to . ok is false if (no exact power of ten). Since doubles of that size are integers (their spacing is 2 or more), the\nrounded product or quotient is an integer, and only its exact rounding error\nhas to be added (rounded). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=dp), intent(in) :: a integer, intent(in) :: k integer(kind=int64), intent(out) :: im logical, intent(out) :: ok Calls proc~~scaled~~CallsGraph proc~scaled scaled proc~two_prod two_prod proc~scaled->proc~two_prod proc~split split proc~two_prod->proc~split Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Called by proc~~sca