o , rho1 , rho2 !! rho_n and its first and second derivatives w.r.t. r real ( wp ) :: bn !! B_n = sum_m A(n,m) D(n,m) real ( wp ) :: c , sn !! C(n,m), S(n,m) real ( wp ) :: d , ds , dt , dss , dst !! D(n,m) = C r_m + S i_m, and its derivatives w.r.t. s and t real ( wp ) :: sg !! shat . g integer :: n , m , mtop , i , j logical :: need_grad need_grad = present ( grad ) rmag = norm2 ( r ) rinv = one / rmag shat = r * rinv s = shat ( 1 ) t = shat ( 2 ) u = shat ( 3 ) ! derived Legendre functions A(n,m) (zero for m > n): a = zero a ( 0 , 0 ) = one if ( nmax >= 1 ) then a ( 1 , 0 ) = u a ( 1 , 1 ) = one end if do n = 2 , nmax a ( n , 0 ) = ( real ( 2 * n - 1 , wp ) * u * a ( n - 1 , 0 ) - real ( n - 1 , wp ) * a ( n - 2 , 0 )) / real ( n , wp ) do m = 1 , n ! from P'_n - P'_{n-2} = (2n-1) P_{n-1}, differentiated m-1 times: a ( n , m ) = real ( 2 * n - 1 , wp ) * a ( n - 1 , m - 1 ) + a ( n - 2 , m ) end do end do ! (s + i t)&#94;m: rm ( 0 ) = one im ( 0 ) = zero do m = 1 , nmax rm ( m ) = s * rm ( m - 1 ) - t * im ( m - 1 ) im ( m ) = s * im ( m - 1 ) + t * rm ( m - 1 ) end do ! accumulate U_r, U_rr, g, g_r, G_ss: ur = zero urr = zero g = zero gr = zero gss = zero rho = mu * rinv ! rho_0 do n = 0 , nmax if ( n == 1 ) then ! degree 1 is zero (center of mass at the origin) rho = rho * re * rinv cycle end if rho1 = - real ( n + 1 , wp ) * rho * rinv rho2 = real (( n + 1 ) * ( n + 2 ), wp ) * rho * rinv * rinv bn = zero bn_g = zero bn_h = zero if ( n == 0 ) then bn = one ! the central term (C00 = 1) else mtop = min ( n , mmax ) do m = 0 , mtop c = cnm ( n , m ) sn = snm ( n , m ) d = c * rm ( m ) + sn * im ( m ) if ( m >= 1 ) then ds = real ( m , wp ) * ( c * rm ( m - 1 ) + sn * im ( m - 1 )) dt = real ( m , wp ) * ( sn * rm ( m - 1 ) - c * im ( m - 1 )) else ds = zero dt = zero end if bn = bn + a ( n , m ) * d bn_g ( 1 ) = bn_g ( 1 ) + a ( n , m ) * ds bn_g ( 2 ) = bn_g ( 2 ) + a ( n , m ) * dt bn_g ( 3 ) = bn_g ( 3 ) + a ( n , m + 1 ) * d if ( need_grad ) then if ( m >= 2 ) then dss = real ( m * ( m - 1 ), wp ) * ( c * rm ( m - 2 ) + sn * im ( m - 2 )) dst = real ( m * ( m - 1 ), wp ) * ( sn * rm ( m - 2 ) - c * im ( m - 2 )) else dss = zero dst = zero end if bn_h ( 1 , 1 ) = bn_h ( 1 , 1 ) + a ( n , m ) * dss bn_h ( 1 , 2 ) = bn_h ( 1 , 2 ) + a ( n , m ) * dst bn_h ( 2 , 2 ) = bn_h ( 2 , 2 ) - a ( n , m ) * dss ! (D_tt = -D_ss) bn_h ( 1 , 3 ) = bn_h ( 1 , 3 ) + a ( n , m + 1 ) * ds bn_h ( 2 , 3 ) = bn_h ( 2 , 3 ) + a ( n , m + 1 ) * dt bn_h ( 3 , 3 ) = bn_h ( 3 , 3 ) + a ( n , m + 2 ) * d end if end do end if ur = ur + rho1 * bn urr = urr + rho2 * bn g = g + rho * bn_g gr = gr + rho1 * bn_g if ( need_grad ) gss = gss + rho * bn_h rho = rho * re * rinv ! rho_{n+1} end do ! acceleration: sg = dot_product ( shat , g ) pg = g - sg * shat acc = ur * shat + rinv * pg if ( need_grad ) then gss ( 2 , 1 ) = gss ( 1 , 2 ) gss ( 3 , 1 ) = gss ( 1 , 3 ) gss ( 3 , 2 ) = gss ( 2 , 3 ) p = - outer ( shat , shat ) do i = 1 , 3 p ( i , i ) = p ( i , i ) + one end do pgr = gr - dot_product ( shat , gr ) * shat grad = urr * outer ( shat , shat ) & + rinv * ( outer ( pgr , shat ) + outer ( shat , pgr )) & + ( ur * rinv ) * p & + ( rinv * rinv ) * ( matmul ( p , matmul ( gss , p )) - ( outer ( pg , shat ) + outer ( shat , pg )) - sg * p ) ! symmetrize (it is symmetric analytically): do j = 1 , 3 do i = j + 1 , 3 grad ( i , j ) = 0.5_wp * ( grad ( i , j ) + grad ( j , i )) grad ( j , i ) = grad ( i , j ) end do end do end if end subroutine pines_gravity","tags":"","url":"proc/pines_gravity.html"},{"title":"two_body_rotating_frame_matrices – halo","text":"public pure subroutine two_body_rotating_frame_matrices(rv, rdot, vdot, m, mdot, n, ndot) The 6x6 state transformations of a two-body rotating frame (as defined by the\ntoolkit's two_body_rotating_frame ), and their exact time derivatives. The frame's axes are , ( ), , where is the secondary body's state w.r.t. the primary body.\nWith the matrix whose rows are the axes, and (as in the toolkit) , : inertial to rotating: , rotating to inertial: . (Both frames are assumed to have the same origin.) The time derivatives of and are computed exactly from the time derivatives of and ( rdot , vdot ). Note that is\nthe toolkit's definition, which is not exactly (it neglects the\nrotation of ); the derivatives here are of the transformation as\nit is actually defined. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(in), dimension(6) :: rv state of the secondary w.r.t. the primary [km, km/s] real(kind=wp), intent(in), dimension(3) :: rdot time derivative of rv(1:3) [km/s] real(kind=wp), intent(in), dimension(3) :: vdot time derivative of rv(4:6) [km/s&#94;2] real(kind=wp), intent(out), optional, dimension(6,6) :: m inertial to rotating real(kind=wp), intent(out), optional, dimension(6,6) :: mdot dM/dt [1/s] real(kind=wp), intent(out), optional, dimension(6,6) :: n rotating to inertial real(kind=wp), intent(out), optional, dimension(6,6) :: ndot dN/dt [1/s] Calls proc~~two_body_rotating_frame_matrices~~CallsGraph proc~two_body_rotating_frame_matrices two_body_rotating_frame_matrices proc~cross cross proc~two_body_rotating_frame_matrices->proc~cross proc~cross_matrix cross_matrix proc~two_body_rotating_frame_matrices->proc~cross_matrix Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Called by proc~~two_body_rotating_frame_matrices~~CalledByGraph proc~two_body_rotating_frame_matrices two_body_rotating_frame_matrices proc~earth_moon_frame_matrices earth_m