rameters_module module~halo_eclipse_opt_submodule halo_eclipse_opt_submodule module~halo_eclipse_opt_submodule->module~halo_module Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Module Module Submodule Submodule Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a submodule to the (sub)module which it is\ndescended from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial integer, public, parameter :: wp = real64 Real working precision if not specified [8 bytes]","tags":"","url":"module/halo_kinds_module.html"},{"title":"splined_moon_frame_module – halo","text":"Splined lunar principal-axis (MOON_PA) frame: the rotation from J2000 to the\nframe, interpolated from a table of the frame's roll, pitch and yaw angles vs.\nephemeris time (e.g., data/moon_pa_2000_2100.csv , generated with SPICE). This is the same interpolation as the moonframe library's moon_frame_interpolater (quartic B-splines of the roll, the pitch, and the\ncosine and sine of the yaw angle, with the same knots), and gives identical\nresults, but with the same pattern as splined_ephemeris_module : the spline\ncoefficients are global variables, computed once and then only read, so all\nthe segments (and threads) share one copy. Each moon_pa_frame object only\nholds its own small evaluation workspace (the interval indices and a work\narray, which db1val modifies), so each segment (thread) has its own.\n(With a copy of the coefficients in every segment, the memory grew with the\nsquare of the number of revolutions.) Uses halo_kinds_module bspline_module csv_module module~~splined_moon_frame_module~~UsesGraph module~splined_moon_frame_module splined_moon_frame_module bspline_module bspline_module module~splined_moon_frame_module->bspline_module csv_module csv_module module~splined_moon_frame_module->csv_module module~halo_kinds_module halo_kinds_module module~splined_moon_frame_module->module~halo_kinds_module iso_fortran_env iso_fortran_env module~halo_kinds_module->iso_fortran_env Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Module Module Submodule Submodule Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a submodule to the (sub)module which it is\ndescended from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. Used by module~~splined_moon_frame_module~~UsedByGraph module~splined_moon_frame_module splined_moon_frame_module module~halo_module halo_module module~halo_module->module~splined_moon_frame_module module~halo_eclipse_opt_submodule halo_eclipse_opt_submodule module~halo_eclipse_opt_submodule->module~halo_module Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Module Module Submodule Submodule Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a submodule to the (sub)module which it is\ndescended from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial integer, private, parameter :: kx = bspline_order_quartic spline order (as in moonframe ) integer, private, parameter :: iknot = 0 knots chosen by db1ink (as in moonframe ) integer, private, parameter :: n_splines = 4 roll, pitch, cos(yaw), sin(yaw) integer, private :: nx = 0 number of points real(kind=wp), private, dimension(:,:), allocatable :: tx (nx+kx, n_splines) knots real(kind=wp), private, dimension(:,:), allocatable :: bcoef (nx, n_splines) coefficients Derived Types type, public :: moon_pa_frame The interface to the splined MOON_PA frame: only the evaluation workspace\n(the splines themselves are global). Make a copy for each thread. Components Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial integer, private, dimension(n_splines) :: inbvx = 1