to generate the python plots logical, public :: generate_trajectory_files = .true. to export the txt trajectory files. logical, public :: generate_json_trajectory_file = .false. to export the JSON trajectory file for the solution\n(contains inertial and rotating data). This one is used\nby the PyVista python script for plotting logical, public :: generate_guess_and_solution_files = .true. to export the json guess and solution files. logical, public :: generate_kernel = .false. to generate a spice kernel (bsp) of the solution\n[this requires the external mkspk SPICE tool] logical, public :: generate_solution_plots = .false. write the solution's plot data ( solution_plot_data_*.json :\nthe epochs and defects at the constraint points, for the\ninitial guess and the solution) and run python/plot_solution.py on it (matplotlib: the epoch\ndrift and defect plots, *.pdf and *.png ) logical, public :: generate_defect_file = .false. generate the file that shows the pos/vel\nconstraint defects for the solution logical, public :: generate_eclipse_files = .false. generate the eclipse data file for the solution logical, public :: run_pyvista_script = .false. run the pyvista script to generate the interacdtive 3d plot logical, public :: generate_rp_ra_file = .false. to generate the rp_ra file real(kind=wp), public :: r_eclipse_bubble = 0.0_wp radius of the \"eclipse bubble\" [km] logical, public :: eclipse_optimization = .false. after the solve, move the solution out of the Earth's shadow:\nthe closest continuous trajectory with the shadow function at\nleast eclipse_opt_phi_min near the eclipses (solved with sqpopt) real(kind=wp), public :: eclipse_opt_phi_min = 0.05_wp the shadow function required at the constraint samples (>0: a margin) real(kind=wp), public :: eclipse_opt_bubble = 0.0_wp eclipse bubble radius for the constraints [km] real(kind=wp), public :: eclipse_opt_detect_phi = 0.3_wp segments whose shadow function falls below this get an eclipse constraint real(kind=wp), public :: eclipse_opt_detect_step = 300.0_wp time step for checking the shadow function along the trajectory [sec] real(kind=wp), public :: eclipse_opt_sample_step = 300.0_wp spacing of the constraint samples [sec] integer, public :: eclipse_opt_max_outer = 3 maximum number of passes (find the eclipses, optimize, check) logical, public :: eclipse_opt_polish = .false. re-converge the continuity with the Newton solver after each optimization\n(continuity only: only for a converged optimization, whose point is\nalready feasible; from an unconverged one it undoes the eclipse fix) logical, public :: eclipse_opt_newton_finish = .true. after each optimization, a Newton solve of the continuity\nconstraints and, as equalities (KS = eclipse_opt_phi_min ), the\neclipse rows that are at or near their bound (see eclipse_opt_newton_active_tol ): converges the continuity\nwithout undoing the eclipse fix real(kind=wp), public :: eclipse_opt_newton_active_tol = 0.02_wp the Newton finish's equalities: the eclipse rows with\nKS below eclipse_opt_phi_min plus this (a row that\nfalls below its bound in the finish is added, and\nthe finish repeated) integer, public :: eclipse_opt_newton_max_iter = 50 maximum number of iterations of each Newton finish integer, public :: eclipse_opt_newton_solver_mode = 0 the Newton finish's sparse linear solver (nlesolver's sparsity_mode : 2-4, 6 or 7); 0: halo's solver_mode real(kind=wp), public :: eclipse_opt_newton_damp = 1.0e-4_wp the Newton finish's first damping (nlesolver's damp : LSQR,\nLSMR, CRAIG and the Cholesky solver). The eclipse rows at\ntheir bound are nearly dependent on the continuity rows, so\nthe undamped steps are long and fail: the finish is done in\nstages, the damping divided by 10 each stage, to 0 integer, public :: eclipse_opt_newton_damp_iter = 3 maximum number of iterations of each damped stage integer, public :: eclipse_opt_objective = 1 the optimization's objective: 1 - |x - x0|&#94;2/2 (the closest\nsolution to the start); 0 - none (a feasibility problem, as\nSNOPT's feasible point mode) logical, public :: sqpopt_solve = .false. TEMPORARY experiment: solve the problem with sqpopt (as the eclipse\noptimization, with no eclipse rows) instead of nlesolver integer, public :: eclipse_opt_newton_max_active = -1 TEMPORARY experiment: hold only this many rows (the smallest KS); <0: off real(kind=wp), public :: eclipse_opt_newton_damp_min = 1.0e-9_wp below this, the damping is 0 (the last stage) real(kind=wp), public :: eclipse_opt_fd_step = 1.0e-6_wp central-difference step for the eclipse constraint rows (scaled variables) real(kind=wp), public :: eclipse_opt_max_step_epoch = -1.0_wp largest change of a node epoch in one sqpopt iteration [days]\n(sqpopt's set_max_step; <=0: no limit) real(kind=wp), public :: eclipse_opt_max_step_position = -1.0_wp largest change of a node position component [km] (<=0: no limit) real(kind=wp), public :: eclipse_opt_max_step_velocity = -1.0_wp largest change of a node velocity component [km/s] (<=0: no limit) logical, public :: eclipse_opt_equilibrate = .false. solve the optimization with the continuity Jacobian equilibrated\n(its rows and columns normalized, at the converged solution),\nwhich lowers the condition number of sqpopt's QP subproblems.\nThe objective is then measured in those units logical, public :: eclipse_opt_single_row = .false. one eclipse constraint for all the segments near the shadow\n(the KS aggregate of the segments' rows: exactly the KS of all\ntheir samples), instead of one per segment real(kind=wp), public :: eclipse_opt_ks_rho = 100.0_wp the KS aggregate's parameter: the constraint is within ln(N)/rho\nof the smallest of a segment's N samples (and below it) integer, public :: eclipse_opt_max_iter = 100 integer, public :: eclipse_opt_print_level = 1 integer, public :: eclipse_opt_hessian_mode = 1 1: BFGS, 2: SR1 logical, public :: eclipse_opt_direct_qp = .true. logical, public :: eclipse_opt_direct_least_squares = .true. real(kind=wp), public :: eclipse_opt_direct_tol = 1.0e-8_wp sqpopt qp_solver%direct_tol: the direct QP method's relative tolerance\nfor a violated row (and for the working set's rows) logical, public :: eclipse_opt_direct_relative_tol = .false. sqpopt qp_solver%direct_relative_tol logical, public :: eclipse_opt_direct_accept_inexact = .false. sqpopt qp_solver%direct_accept_inexact logical, public :: eclipse_opt_basis_repair = .false. sqpopt qp_solver%sparse_qp%basis_repair real(kind=wp), public :: eclipse_opt_basis_rel_tol = 1.0e-8_wp sqpopt qp_solver%sparse_qp%basis_rel_tol real(kind=wp), public :: eclipse_opt_basis_eq_slack_weight = 1.0e-6_wp sqpopt qp_solver%sparse_qp%basis_eq_slack_weight integer, public :: eclipse_opt_linear_solver = 2 sqpopt linear_solver: 1 MUMPS (needs a build with HAS_MUMPS),\n2 QDLDL (the default), 3 dense, 4 LAPACK (see\nsqpopt_symmetric_solver_module) integer, public :: eclipse_opt_factorization_threads = 1 sqpopt factorization_threads (MUMPS only) integer, public :: eclipse_opt_direct_max_changes = 1000 sqpopt qp_solver%direct_max_changes: changes of the working set\nthe direct QP method may make before it gives up integer, public :: eclipse_opt_qp_solver_mode = 0 0: auto, 2: dense, 3: sparse (reduced Hessian), 4: DAQP integer, public :: eclipse_opt_linesearch_mode = 4 1: Armijo, 2: exact, 3: watchdog, 4: filter, 5: funnel integer, public :: eclipse_opt_lbfgs_memory = 0 real(kind=wp), public :: eclipse_opt_elastic_multiplier_limit = 0.0_wp sqpopt elastic_multiplier_limit (0: no elastic\nre-solves, which skip the direct QP method) logical, public :: eclipse_opt_scaling = .false. (halo's variables and constraints are already scaled) real(kind=wp), public :: eclipse_opt_scaling_max_gradient = 100.0_wp real(kind=wp), public :: eclipse_opt_hessian_scale0 = 1.0_wp logical, public :: eclipse_opt_inertia_control = .false. integer, public :: eclipse_opt_merit_mode = 1 1: l1, 2: augmented Lagrangian integer, public :: eclipse_opt_restoration_mode = 1 1: restor