ps (for plotting) real(kind=wp), intent(in), optional :: tstep fixed time step for mode=2 public  subroutine propagate_segment_stm (me) Propagate a segment with its state transition matrix, and compute the analytic\npartials of its final rotating-frame state (for jacobian_mode=2 ): Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( segment ), intent(inout) :: me public  subroutine earth_moon_frame_matrices (seg, et, m, mdot, n, ndot) The Moon-centered Earth-Moon rotating frame transformations at et (and their\ntime derivatives), consistent with the toolkit's two_body_rotating_frame as used in set_segment_inputs and propagate_segment .\nRequires the splined ephemeris (for the time derivatives). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( segment ), intent(inout) :: seg real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: et ephemeris time [sec] real(kind=wp), intent(out), optional, dimension(6,6) :: m inertial to rotating real(kind=wp), intent(out), optional, dimension(6,6) :: mdot dm/dt real(kind=wp), intent(out), optional, dimension(6,6) :: n rotating to inertial real(kind=wp), intent(out), optional, dimension(6,6) :: ndot dn/dt public  subroutine segs_to_propagate (me, funcs_to_compute, isegs_to_propagate) Given the functions to be computed, returns the segments that need to be propagated. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( mission_type ), intent(inout) :: me integer, intent(in), optional, dimension(:) :: funcs_to_compute the indices of f to compute integer, intent(out), dimension(:), allocatable :: isegs_to_propagate segment numbers public  subroutine constraint_violations (me, x, f, funcs_to_compute) Computes the constraint violation vector for the mission. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( mission_type ), intent(inout) :: me real(kind=wp), intent(in), dimension(:) :: x opt var vector for the mission [n] real(kind=wp), intent(out), dimension(:) :: f constraint violation vector for the mission [m] integer, intent(in), option