iable scaling r . Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( eclipse_opt_data ), intent(in) :: d real(kind=wp), intent(inout), dimension(:) :: jac subroutine find_rows (mission, x, rows, phimin, shadow_min) Check the shadow function along the whole trajectory (every eclipse_opt_detect_step seconds), and make the rows of the segments that come near the shadow (where the shadow\nfunction, with the constraints' bubble, is below eclipse_opt_detect_phi ). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( mission_type ), intent(inout) :: mission real(kind=wp), intent(in), dimension(:) :: x type( eclipse_row ), intent(out), dimension(:), allocatable :: rows real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: phimin the smallest shadow function (no bubble) along the trajectory real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: shadow_min the time in the shadow [min] (approximate: the number of points\nin the shadow times the step) subroutine row_columns (iseg, full2red, row) The variables a row of segment iseg depends on: the epoch and state of its start node. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: iseg integer, intent(in), dimension(:) :: full2red type( eclipse_row ), intent(inout) :: row subroutine merge_rows (rows, new) Add the new rows: a segment already in the list gets the union of the sample ranges. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( eclipse_row ), intent(inout), dimension(:), allocatable :: rows type( eclipse_row ), intent(in), dimension(:) :: new subroutine report_change (mission, x0, x) Print how far the optimization moved the solution. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( mission_type ), intent(inout) :: mission real(kind=wp), intent(in), dimension(:) :: x0 real(kind=wp), intent(in), dimension(:) :: x Module Subroutines module subroutine eclipse_optimize (me, x) Interface → Move a converged solution out of the Earth's shadow (see the module documentation). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( my_solver_type ),