urcefile~halo_kinds_module.f90 sourcefile~text_buffer_module.f90->sourcefile~halo_kinds_module.f90 Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Source File Source File This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a file to a file which it depends on. A file\nis dependent upon another if the latter must be compiled before the former\ncan be. Source Code !***************************************************************************************** !> !  Eclipse optimization: moves a converged solution out of the Earth's shadow. ! !  Starting from the converged solution `x0`, it finds the closest continuous trajectory !  (in halo's scaled variables) that stays out of the shadow near the eclipses: ! !  * minimize  \\frac{1}{2} \\lVert \\mathbf{x} - \\mathbf{x}_0 \\rVert&#94;2  !  * subject to the continuity constraints  \\mathbf{c}(\\mathbf{x}) = \\mathbf{0}  (halo's) !  * and, for each segment that comes near the shadow,  \\mathrm{KS}(\\phi_k) \\ge \\phi_{min}  ! !  with the SQP solver [sqpopt](https://github.com/jacobwilliams/sqpopt).  \\phi  is the !  cubic shadow model (Williams et al., 2023), which is smooth inside and outside the !  shadow.  \\phi_k  are its values at samples every `eclipse_opt_sample_step` seconds !  from the segment's start, across the part of the segment near the shadow, and KS is !  their Kreisselmeier-Steinhauser aggregate !   \\mathrm{KS} = \\phi_{lo} - \\frac{1}{\\rho} \\ln \\sum_k e&#94;{-\\rho(\\phi_k - \\phi_{lo})} , !   \\phi_{lo} = \\min_k \\phi_k : a smooth lower bound of the smallest sample (within !   \\ln(N)/\\rho  of it), so the constraint keeps every sample at or above !   \\phi_{min} . One row per segment, not one per sample: the samples of a segment all !  depend on the same few variables (its start node), and a row for each would make the !  QP's working sets dependent (sqpopt's direct method then cycles). ! !  Following the 2023 paper's process, the constraints are added only where the trajectory !  comes near the shadow, and the trajectory is checked again after each optimization (with !  new rows where needed). Each pass ends with a Newton solve of the continuity constraints !  and the eclipse rows at their bound, as equalities (`eclipse_opt_newton_finish`), to !  bring the defects back to the usual level without undoing the eclipse fix. ! !  The continuity rows of the Jacobian are halo's analytic ones. The eclipse rows (7 !  nonzeros each: the epoch and state of the segment's start node; the samples are at fixed !  offsets from the start) are computed by central differences, propagating only that !  segment. ! !  See `docs/eclipse_optimization_plan.md`. submodule ( halo_module ) halo_eclipse_opt_submodule use sqpopt_module , only : sqpopt_type use sqpopt_problem_module , only : sqpopt_problem_type use sqpopt_options_module , only : sqpopt_options_type use sqpopt_qp_solver_module , only : sqpopt_qp_solver_type use sqpopt_types_module , only : sqpopt_infinity , sqpopt_results_type use iso_fortran_env , only : int64 implicit none ! for each of the 8 segments of a rev: its start node, and the node whose epoch sets its final ! epoch (as in [[compute_jacobian_stm]]) integer , dimension ( 8 ), parameter :: start_node = [ 1 , 2 , 2 , 3 , 3 , 4 , 4 , 5 ] integer , dimension ( 8 ), parameter :: tf_node = [ 1 , 1 , 3 , 3 , 3 , 3 , 5 , 5 ] type :: eclipse_row !! an eclipse constraint: the KS aggregate of the shadow function at the samples !! `k_lo` to `k_hi` of a segment (sample `k` is `k*eclipse_opt_sample_step` seconds !! from the segment's start, along its direction of propagation) integer :: iseg = 0 integer :: k_lo = 0 integer :: k_hi = 0 logical :: tf_with_t0 = . false . !! if the segment's final epoch moves with its start node's epoch integer :: ncol = 0 !! number of variables it depends on integer , dimension ( 7 ) :: col = 0 !! their indices in `x` integer , dimension ( 7 ) :: kind = 0 !! 0: the start node's epoch, 1-6: its state end type eclipse_row type :: eclipse_opt_data !! the data the sqpopt functions need type ( mission_type ), pointer :: mission => null () real ( wp ), dimension (:), allocatable :: x0 !! the solution before the optimization (scaled) real ( wp ), dimension (:), allocatable :: r !! the optimization's variables are `x/r` (see `eclipse_opt_epoch_scale`) type ( eclipse_row ), dimension (:), allocatable :: rows integer :: m_halo = 0 !! number of halo's constraints integer , dimension (:), allocatable :: icol !! the columns of halo's Jacobian nonzeros integer , dimension (:), allocatable :: irow !! the rows of halo's Jacobian nonzeros real ( wp ), dimension (:), allocatable :: w !! weights of halo's constraint rows in the optimization !! (see `eclipse_opt_equilibrate`; 1 otherwise) integer :: nnz_halo = 0 !! number of nonzeros of halo's Jacobian logical :: single = . false . !! one eclipse row for all the segments: the KS aggregate of the !! segments' rows (see `eclipse_opt_single_row`) integer , dimension (:), allocatable :: ucol !! with `single`: the row's columns (the union of the segments') integer , dimension (:), allocatable :: upos !! with `single`: the index in `ucol` of each segment row's column end type eclipse_opt_data type , extends ( nlesolver_type ) :: eclipse_newton_type !! the Newton finish (see [[newton_finish]]): halo's continuity constraints, then !! the active eclipse rows as equalities type ( eclipse_opt_data ), pointer :: d => null () integer , dimension (:), allocatable :: active !! the indices in `d%rows` of the rows that are equalities logical , dimension (:), allocatable :: mask !! the same, as a mask of `d%rows` end type eclipse_newton_type contains !***************************************************************************************** !***************************************************************************************** !> !  Move a converged solution out of the Earth's shadow (see the module documentation). module subroutine eclipse_optimize ( me , x ) class ( my_solver_type ), intent ( inout ), target :: me real ( wp ), dimension (:), intent ( inout ) :: x !! the converged solution (scaled); replaced by the result type ( eclipse_opt_data ), target :: d type ( sqpopt_problem_type ) :: problem type ( sqpopt_options_type ) :: options type ( sqpopt_qp_solver_type ) :: qp_solver type ( sqpopt_type ) :: sqp type ( sqpopt_results_type ) :: res type ( eclipse_row ), dimension (:), allocatable :: new real ( wp ), dimension (:), allocatable :: lambda , x_lb , x_ub , c_lb , c_ub , ks , limits integer , dimension (:), allocatable :: irow , icol , irow_all , icol_all integer :: n , m , mt , iouter , istat , k , j , nnz , nr real ( wp ) :: phimin , shadow_min character ( len = :), allocatable :: message integer ( int64 ) :: count0 , count1 , rate associate ( mission => me % mission ) if ( mission % jacobian_mode /= 2 ) error stop 'eclipse optimization requires jacobian_mode=2' call system_clock ( count0 , rate ) d % mission => me % mission call mission % define_problem_size ( n = n , m = m ) d % x0 = x ! the optimization's own scaling of the variables: y = x/r allocate ( d % r ( n )) d % r = one if ( mission % eclipse_opt_epoch_scale > zero ) then where ( mission % x_is_epoch ) d % r = mission % eclipse_opt_epoch_scale / mission % xscale end if d % m_halo = m d % single = mission % eclipse_opt_single_row call mission % get_sparsity_pattern ( irow , icol ) d % nnz_halo = size ( irow ) d % icol = icol d % irow = irow allocate ( d % w ( m )) d % w = one if ( mission % eclipse_opt_equilibrate ) call equilibrate ( d , x ) allocate ( d % rows ( 0 )) mission % segs % soft_fail = . true . ! (a trial point can be far off: an integrator failure is reported to sqpopt) write ( * , '(A)' ) '' write ( * , '(A)' ) ' * Eclipse optimization' if ( mission % sqpopt_solve ) then ! TEMPORARY experiment: solve halo's problem (continuity only) with sqpopt allocate ( new ( 0 )) write ( * , '(A)' ) '   (sqpopt_solve: the continuity constraints only, from the initial guess)' else call find_rows ( mission , x , new , phimin , shadow_min ) write ( * , '(A,F8.4,A,F8.1,A,I0,A)' ) '   converged solution: min phi = ' , phimin , ', ' , shadow_min , & ' min in the shadow, ' , size ( new ), ' segments near the shadow' end if do iouter = 1 , mission % eclipse_opt_max_outer call merge_rows ( d % rows , new ) nr = size ( d % rows ) if ( nr == 0 . and . . not . mission % sqpopt_solve ) then write ( * , '(A)' ) '   nothing near the shadow: no optimization needed' exit end if if ( d % single ) then mt = m + 1 call union_columns ( d ) write ( * , '(A,I0,A,I0,A,I0,A)' ) '   pass ' , iouter , ': 1 eclipse constraint (' , nr , ' segments, ' , & sum ( d % rows % k_hi - d % rows % k_lo + 1 ), ' samples)' else mt = m + nr write ( * , '(A,I0,A,I0,A,I0,A)' ) '   pass ' , iouter , ': ' , nr , ' eclipse constraints (' , & sum ( d % rows % k_hi - d % rows % k_lo + 1 ), ' samples)' end if if ( nr > 0 ) then allocate ( ks ( nr )) call mission % put_x_in_segments ( x ) call eval_rows ( d , ks ) write ( * , '(A,F8.4,A,F8.4)' ) '   smallest eclipse constraint (KS) at the start: ' , minval ( ks ), & ', their aggregate: ' , ks_aggregate ( ks , mission % eclipse_opt_ks_rho ) deallocate ( ks ) end if ! the problem: halo's continuity rows (equalities), then the eclipse rows ! (inequalities, KS >= phi_min) if ( d % single ) then nnz = d % nnz_halo + size ( d % ucol ) else nnz = d % nnz_halo + sum ( d % rows % ncol ) end if allocate ( irow_all ( nnz ), icol_all ( nnz )) irow_all ( 1 : d % nnz_halo ) = irow icol_all ( 1 : d % nnz_halo ) = icol if ( d % single ) then irow_all ( d % nnz_halo + 1 :) = m + 1 icol_all ( d % nnz_halo + 1 :) = d % ucol else j = d % nnz_halo do k = 1 , nr irow_all ( j + 1 : j + d % rows ( k )% ncol ) = m + k icol_all ( j + 1 : j + d % rows ( k )% ncol ) = d % rows ( k )% col ( 1 : d % rows ( k )% ncol ) j = j + d % rows ( k )% ncol end do end if allocate ( x_lb ( n ), x_ub ( n ), c_lb ( mt ), c_ub ( mt ), lambda ( mt )) x_lb = - sqpopt_infinity x_ub = sqpopt_infinity c_lb ( 1 : m ) = zero c_ub ( 1 : m ) = zero c_lb ( m + 1 :) = mission % eclipse_opt_phi_min c_ub ( m + 1 :) = sqpopt_infinity call problem % set_problem_size ( n = n , m = mt ) call problem % set_bounds ( x_lb , x_ub , c_lb , c_ub ) call problem % set_jacobian_sparsity ( nnz , irow_all , icol_all ) call problem % set_functions ( fc = eclipse_fc , gjac = eclipse_gjac , data = d ) if ( mission % eclipse_opt_max_step_epoch > zero . or . mission % eclipse_opt_max_step_position > zero . or . & mission % eclipse_opt_max_step_velocity > zero ) then limits = step_limits ( d ) call problem % set_max_step ( limits ) end if options % max_iter = mission % eclipse_opt_max_iter options % print_level = mission % eclipse_opt_print_level options % hessian_mode = mission % eclipse_opt_hessian_mode options % direct_qp = mission % eclipse_opt_direct_qp options % direct_least_squares = mission % eclipse_opt_direct_least_squares options % qp_solver_mode = mission % eclipse_opt_qp_solver_mode options % linesearch_mode = mission % eclipse_opt_linesearch_mode options % lbfgs_memory = mission % eclipse_opt_lbfgs_memory options % scaling = mission % eclipse_opt_scaling options % ctol = mission % eclipse_opt_ctol options % ktol = mission % eclipse_opt_ktol options % elastic_multiplier_limit = mission % eclipse_opt_elastic_multiplier_limit options % scaling_max_gradient = mission % eclipse_opt_scaling_max_gradient options % hessian_scale0 = mission % eclipse_opt_hessian_scale0 options % inertia_control = mission % eclipse_opt_inertia_control options % merit_mode = mission % eclipse_opt_merit_mode options % restoration_mode = mission % eclipse_opt_restoration_mode options % max_time = mission % eclipse_opt_max_time options % linear_solver = mission % eclipse_opt_linear_solver options % factorization_threads = mission % eclipse_opt_factorization_threads qp_solver % max_step = mission % eclipse_opt_qp_max_step qp_solver % direct_max_changes = mission % eclipse_opt_direct_max_changes qp_solver % direct_tol = mission % eclipse_opt_direct_tol qp_solver % sparse_qp % basis_rel_tol = mission % eclipse_opt_basis_rel_tol qp_solver % sparse_qp % basis_repair = mission % eclipse_opt_basis_repair qp_solver % sparse_qp % basis_eq_slack_weight = mission % eclipse_opt_basis_eq_slack_weight qp_solver % direct_relative_tol = mission % eclipse_opt_direct_relative_tol qp_solver % direct_accept_inexact = mission % eclipse_opt_direct_accept_inexact call sqp % initialize ( problem = problem , options = options , qp_solver = qp_solver ) call sqp % solve ( x / d % r , istat ) call sqp % get_solution ( x , lambda ) x = x * d % r call sqp % get_results ( res ) write ( * , '(A)' ) '   sqpopt: ' // sqp % status_message () write ( * , '(A,I0,A,I0,A,I0,A,ES10.3,A,ES10.3,A,F9.2,A)' ) '   sqpopt: ' , res % iterations , ' iterations, ' , & res % n_eval_fc , ' fc, ' , res % n_eval_gjac , ' gjac, f = ' , res % f , ', infeasibility = ' , & res % feasibility_error , ', ' , res % time , ' s' call sqp % destroy () deallocate ( irow_all , icol_all , x_lb , x_ub , c_lb , c_ub , lambda ) if ( mission % sqpopt_solve ) then ! TEMPORARY experiment: how well sqpopt alone converged halo's problem block real ( wp ), dimension (:), allocatable :: c allocate ( c ( m )) call mission % constraint_violations ( x , c ) ! (propagates the segments at x) write ( * , '(A,ES12.4,A,ES12.4,A,ES10.2)' ) '   sqpopt_solve: halo''s constraint norm ' , norm2 ( c ), & ', largest |c| ' , maxval ( abs ( c )), ' (nlesolver_tol ' , mission % nlesolver_tol end block exit end if ! converge the continuity, with the eclipse rows at their bound held there: if ( mission % eclipse_opt_newton_finish ) call newton_finish ( d , x ) ! re-converge the continuity (only): if ( mission % eclipse_opt_polish ) then write ( * , '(A)' ) '   polish (Newton, continuity only):' call me % solve ( x ) call me % status ( istat = istat , message = message ) write ( * , '(A)' ) '   polish: ' // message end if ! check the whole trajectory: call find_rows ( mission , x , new , phimin , shadow_min ) write ( * , '(A,I0,A,F8.4,A,F8.1,A)' ) '   after pass ' , iouter , ': min phi = ' , phimin , ', ' , & shadow_min , ' min in the shadow' if ( phimin >= zero ) then write ( * , '(A)' ) '   eclipse free' exit end if end do mission % segs % soft_fail = . false . call report_change ( mission , d % x0 , x ) call system_clock ( count1 ) write ( * , '(A,F10.2,A)' ) '   eclipse optimization wall time: ' , real ( count1 - count0 , wp ) / real ( rate , wp ), ' s' write ( * , '(A)' ) '' end associate end subroutine eclipse_optimize !***************************************************************************************** !***************************************************************************************** !> !  The objective and the constraints for sqpopt: halo's continuity constraints, then the !  eclipse rows. subroutine eclipse_fc ( x , f , c , status , data ) real ( wp ), dimension (:), intent ( in ) :: x real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: f real ( wp ), dimension (:), intent ( out ) :: c integer , intent ( inout ) :: status class ( * ), optional , intent ( inout ) :: data real ( wp ), dimension (:), allocatable :: ks logical :: ok if (. not . present ( data )) error stop 'eclipse_fc: no data' select type ( data ) type is ( eclipse_opt_data ) ! (x here is the optimization's variable y = x/r) if ( data % mission % eclipse_opt_objective == 0 ) then f = zero ! (a feasibility problem: as SNOPT's feasible point mode) else f = 0.5_wp * sum (( x - data % x0 / data % r ) ** 2 ) end if if (. not . epochs_in_range ( data , x * data % r )) then c = zero status = 1 ! (outside the splined ephemeris: can't evaluate here) return end if call data % mission % constraint_violations ( x * data % r , c ( 1 : data % m_halo )) ! (also puts x in the segments) c ( 1 : data % m_halo ) = c ( 1 : data % m_halo ) * data % w if ( data % single ) then allocate ( ks ( size ( data % rows ))) call eval_rows ( data , ks , ok = ok ) c ( data % m_halo + 1 ) = ks_aggregate ( ks , data % mission % eclipse_opt_ks_rho ) else call eval_rows ( data , c ( data % m_halo + 1 :), ok = ok ) end if if (. not . ok . or . any ( data % mission % segs % failed )) status = 1 ! (can't evaluate here: sqpopt shortens the step) class default error stop 'eclipse_fc: invalid data' end select end subroutine eclipse_fc !***************************************************************************************** !***************************************************************************************** !> !  The gradient of the objective and the Jacobian values for sqpopt: halo's analytic !  Jacobian, then the eclipse rows (central differences). subroutine eclipse_gjac ( x , g , jac_val , accuracy , status , data ) real ( wp ), dimension (:), intent ( in ) :: x real ( wp ), dimension (:), intent ( out ) :: g real ( wp ), dimension (:), intent ( out ) :: jac_val integer , intent ( in ) :: accuracy integer , intent ( inout ) :: status class ( * ), optional , intent ( inout ) :: data real ( wp ), dimension (:), allocatable :: jac , ks , jr , w real ( wp ) :: rho , kmin integer :: k , j , o logical :: ok if (. not . present ( data )) error stop 'eclipse_gjac: no data' select type ( data ) type is ( eclipse_opt_data ) ! (x here is the optimization's variable y = x/r: the columns are multiplied by r) if ( data % mission % eclipse_opt_objective == 0 ) then g = zero else g = x - data % x0 / data % r end if if (. not . epochs_in_range ( data , x * data % r )) then jac_val = zero status = 1 return end if call data % mission % compute_jacobian_stm ( x * data % r , jac ) ! (also puts x in the segments) jac_val ( 1 : data % nnz_halo ) = jac * data % r ( data % icol ) * data % w ( data % irow ) allocate ( ks ( size ( data % rows )), jr ( sum ( data % rows % ncol ))) call eval_rows ( data , ks , jr , ok = ok ) if (. not . ok . or . any ( data % mission % segs % failed )) status = 1 call scale_row_columns ( data , jr ) if ( data % single ) then ! the aggregate's partials: the segment rows' partials, weighted by d(KS)/d(ks_k) rho = data % mission % eclipse_opt_ks_rho kmin = minval ( ks ) w = exp ( - rho * ( ks - kmin )) w = w / sum ( w ) jac_val ( data % nnz_halo + 1 :) = zero o = 0 do k = 1 , size ( data % rows ) do j = 1 , data % rows ( k )% ncol jac_val ( data % nnz_halo + data % upos ( o + j )) = jac_val ( data % nnz_halo + data % upos ( o + j )) + w ( k ) * jr ( o + j ) end do o = o + data % rows ( k )% ncol end do else jac_val ( data % nnz_halo + 1 :) = jr end if class default error stop 'eclipse_gjac: invalid data' end select end subroutine eclipse_gjac !***************************************************************************************** !***************************************************************************************** !> !  The eclipse rows (and, optionally, their partials, in the order of the rows' columns), !  for the `x` already in the segments. The rows (segments) are done in parallel. subroutine eval_rows ( d , ks , jac , ok , only ) type ( eclipse_opt_data ), intent ( inout ) :: d real ( wp ), dimension (:), intent ( out ) :: ks real ( wp ), dimension (:), intent ( out ), optional :: jac logical , intent ( out ), optional :: ok !! false if a row couldn't be evaluated (see [[row_ks]]) logical , dimension (:), intent ( in ), optional :: only !! evaluate only these rows (the others' `ks` are 0, !! and their partials are not set) integer :: k , j , offset integer , dimension (:), allocatable :: first_nz !! index in `jac` of each row's first nonzero, minus 1 real ( wp ) :: t0 , tf , dt , h , fp , fm real ( wp ), dimension ( 6 ) :: x0r , xp real ( wp ) :: tp0 , tpf logical :: ok_k , all_ok allocate ( first_nz ( size ( d % rows ))) offset = 0 do k = 1 , size ( d % rows ) first_nz ( k ) = offset offset = offset + d % rows ( k )% ncol end do h = d % mission % eclipse_opt_fd_step all_ok = . true . !$OMP PARALLEL DO PRIVATE(k,j,t0,tf,dt,x0r,xp,tp0,tpf,fp,fm,ok_k) SCHEDULE(dynamic) do k = 1 , size ( d % rows ) if ( present ( only )) then if (. not . only ( k )) then ks ( k ) = zero cycle end if end if associate ( row => d % rows ( k ), seg => d % mission % segs ( d % rows ( k )% iseg )) t0 = seg % data % t0 tf = seg % data % tf x0r = seg % data % x0_rotating ks ( k ) = row_ks ( d % mission , seg , row , t0 , tf , x0r , ok_k ) if (. not . ok_k ) all_ok = . false . if ( present ( jac )) then do j = 1 , row % ncol dt = h * d % mission % xscale ( row % col ( j )) ! the unscaled change [days, km or km/s] call perturbed ( row , j , t0 , tf , x0r , + dt , tp0 , tpf , xp ) fp = row_ks ( d % mission , seg , row , tp0 , tpf , xp , ok_k ) if (. not . ok_k ) all_ok = . false . call perturbed ( row , j , t0 , tf , x0r , - dt , tp0 , tpf , xp ) fm = row_ks ( d % mission , seg , row , tp0 , tpf , xp , ok_k ) if (. not . ok_k ) all_ok = . false . jac ( first_nz ( k ) + j ) = ( fp - fm ) / ( 2.0_wp * h ) end do end if end associate end do !$OMP END PARALLEL DO if ( present ( ok )) ok = all_ok contains pure subroutine perturbed ( row , j , t0 , tf , x0r , delta , tp0 , tpf , xp ) !! the segment's inputs with variable `j` of the row changed by `delta` !! (everything is passed in: an internal procedure would see the host's !! variables, not the OpenMP thread's private copies) type ( eclipse_row ), intent ( in ) :: row integer , intent ( in ) :: j real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: t0 , tf , delta real ( wp ), dimension ( 6 ), intent ( in ) :: x0r real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: tp0 , tpf real ( wp ), dimension ( 6 ), intent ( out ) :: xp tp0 = t0 ; tpf = tf ; xp = x0r select case ( row % kind ( j )) case ( 0 ) tp0 = t0 + delta if ( row % tf_with_t0 ) tpf = tf + delta case ( 1 : 6 ) xp ( row % kind ( j )) = x0r ( row % kind ( j )) + delta end select end subroutine perturbed end subroutine eval_rows !***************************************************************************************** !***************************************************************************************** !> !  The Newton finish (`eclipse_opt_newton_finish`): from the optimization's point, solve !  halo's continuity constraints and, as equalities  \\mathrm{KS}_k = \\phi_{min} , the !  eclipse rows that are at or near their bound ( \\mathrm{KS}_k < \\phi_{min}  plus !  `eclipse_opt_newton_active_tol`), with halo's minimum-norm Newton solver (nlesolver, with !  halo's sparse linear solver). The optimization's point is near feasible but its !  continuity isn't converged; a solve of the continuity alone (`eclipse_opt_polish`) moves !  the trajectory back into the shadow, but with the active rows held at their bound it !  can't. A row left free that falls below its bound is added to the equalities, and the !  solve repeated (from where it ended). subroutine newton_finish ( d , x ) type ( eclipse_opt_data ), intent ( inout ), target :: d real ( wp ), dimension (:), intent ( inout ) :: x !! the optimization's point (halo's scaled variables); replaced by the solution type ( eclipse_newton_type ) :: nle real ( wp ), dimension (:), allocatable :: ks integer , dimension (:), allocatable :: irow , icol , irow_all , icol_all logical , dimension (:), allocatable :: is_active , below integer :: attempt , n , m , na , k , j , nnz , istat , mode , stage_iter real ( wp ) :: phi_min , damp , fnorm0 , fnorm real ( wp ), dimension (:), allocatable :: fvec , x_save character ( len = :), allocatable :: message integer ( int64 ) :: count0 , count1 , rate associate ( mission => d % mission ) call system_clock ( count0 , rate ) n = size ( x ) m = d % m_halo phi_min = mission % eclipse_opt_phi_min call mission % get_sparsity_pattern ( irow , icol ) mode = mission % solver_mode if ( mission % eclipse_opt_newton_solver_mode > 0 ) mode = mission % eclipse_opt_newton_solver_mode if ( all ( mode /= [ 2 , 3 , 4 , 6 , 7 ])) mode = 7 ! (a sparse solver of nlesolver's own) allocate ( ks ( size ( d % rows )), is_active ( size ( d % rows )), below ( size ( d % rows ))) call mission % put_x_in_segments ( x ) call eval_rows ( d , ks ) is_active = ks < phi_min + mission % eclipse_opt_newton_active_tol block ! TEMPORARY experiment: hold only the eclipse_opt_newton_max_active rows with the smallest KS integer :: kk , imin real ( wp ), dimension (:), allocatable :: kt if ( mission % eclipse_opt_newton_max_active >= 0 ) then is_active = . false . kt = ks do kk = 1 , min ( mission % eclipse_opt_newton_max_active , size ( ks )) imin = minloc ( kt , 1 ) is_active ( imin ) = . true . kt ( imin ) = huge ( one ) end do end if end block write ( * , '(A,*(F10.6))' ) '   Newton finish: the rows'' KS at the start: ' , ks do attempt = 1 , 5 nle % d => d nle % mask = is_active nle % active = pack ([( k , k = 1 , size ( d % rows ))], is_active ) na = size ( nle % active ) write ( * , '(A,I0,A,I0,A)' ) '   Newton finish ' , attempt , ': the continuity and ' , na , & ' eclipse rows (KS = phi_min)' nnz = size ( irow ) + sum ( d % rows ( nle % active )% ncol ) allocate ( irow_all ( nnz ), icol_all ( nnz )) irow_all ( 1 : size ( irow )) = irow icol_all ( 1 : size ( irow )) = icol j = size ( irow ) do k = 1 , na associate ( row => d % rows ( nle % active ( k ))) irow_all ( j + 1 : j + row % ncol ) = m + k icol_all ( j + 1 : j + row % ncol ) = row % col ( 1 : row % ncol ) j = j + row % ncol end associate end do ! the damping stages: from eclipse_opt_newton_damp down by 10 each stage to 0 (a damped ! stage has eclipse_opt_newton_damp_iter iterations; the undamped last one, up to ! eclipse_opt_newton_max_iter). A stage that ends worse than it started is undone. damp = mission % eclipse_opt_newton_damp allocate ( fvec ( m + na )) do stage_iter = mission % eclipse_opt_newton_max_iter if ( damp > zero ) stage_iter = mission % eclipse_opt_newton_damp_iter nle % d => d nle % mask = is_active nle % active = pack ([( k , k = 1 , size ( d % rows ))], is_active ) call nle % initialize ( n = n , & m = m + na , & max_iter = stage_iter , & func = newton_func , & grad_sparse = newton_grad , & tol = mission % nlesolver_tol , & tolx = mission % nlesolver_tolx , & step_mode = 2 , & ! backtracking (as halo's solve) n_intervals = 2 , & use_broyden = . false ., & export_iteration = newton_export , & sparsity_mode = mode , & atol = 1.0e-12_wp , & btol = 1.0e-12_wp , & damp = damp , & itnlim = 1000000 , & irow = irow_all , & icol = icol_all , & lusol_method = 0 ) call nle % status ( istat = istat , message = message ) if ( istat /= 0 ) then write ( * , '(A)' ) '   Newton finish: ' // message error stop 'error initializing the Newton finish' end if call newton_func ( nle , x , fvec ) fnorm0 = norm2 ( fvec ) x_save = x write ( * , '(A,ES9.1,A,ES12.4)' ) '   Newton finish, damp ' , damp , ': start norm ' , fnorm0 call nle % solve ( x ) call nle % status ( istat = istat , message = message ) call newton_func ( nle , x , fvec ) fnorm = norm2 ( fvec ) write ( * , '(A,ES12.4)' ) '   Newton finish: ' // message // ', norm ' , fnorm if (. not . fnorm <= fnorm0 ) then write ( * , '(A)' ) '   Newton finish: worse; the stage is undone' x = x_save fnorm = fnorm0 end if if ( damp <= zero ) exit if ( fnorm <= mission % nlesolver_tol ) exit ! (converged with damping) damp = damp / 1 0.0_wp if ( damp < mission % eclipse_opt_newton_damp_min ) damp = zero end do call nle % destroy () deallocate ( irow_all , icol_all , fvec ) ! the rows left free must still be at or above their bound: call mission % put_x_in_segments ( x ) call eval_rows ( d , ks ) below = (. not . is_active ) . and . ks < phi_min - 1.0e-6_wp write ( * , '(A,F10.6,A,F10.6,A,I0,A)' ) '   Newton finish: smallest KS ' , minval ( ks ), ' (of the free rows: ' , & minval ( ks , mask = . not . is_active ), '), ' , count ( below ), ' free rows below phi_min' if (. not . any ( below )) exit is_active = is_active . or . below end do call system_clock ( count1 ) write ( * , '(A,F10.2,A)' ) '   Newton finish wall time: ' , real ( count1 - count0 , wp ) / real ( rate , wp ), ' s' end associate end subroutine newton_finish !***************************************************************************************** !***************************************************************************************** !> !  The Newton finish's functions: halo's continuity constraints, then `KS - phi_min` of !  the active eclipse rows. A point that can't be evaluated (outside the splined !  ephemeris, or an integrator failure) gets large values, so the line search backs off. subroutine newton_func ( me , x , f ) class ( nlesolver_type ), intent ( inout ) :: me real ( wp ), dimension (:), intent ( in ) :: x !! halo's scaled variables real ( wp ), dimension (:), intent ( out ) :: f !! the functions real ( wp ), dimension (:), allocatable :: ks integer :: m logical :: ok real ( wp ), parameter :: big = 1.0e10_wp select type ( me ) type is ( eclipse_newton_type ) m = me % d % m_halo if (. not . epochs_in_range ( me % d , x )) then f = big return end if call me % d % mission % constraint_violations ( x , f ( 1 : m )) ! (also puts x in the segments) allocate ( ks ( size ( me % d % rows ))) call eval_rows ( me % d , ks , ok = ok , only = me % mask ) f ( m + 1 :) = ks ( me % active ) - me % d % mission % eclipse_opt_phi_min if (. not . ok . or . any ( me % d % mission % segs % failed )) f = big class default error stop 'newton_func: invalid class' end select end subroutine newton_func !***************************************************************************************** !***************************************************************************************** !> !  The Newton finish's Jacobian: halo's analytic one, then the active eclipse rows !  (central differences, see [[eval_rows]]). subroutine newton_grad ( me , x , g ) class ( nlesolver_type ), intent ( inout ) :: me real ( wp ), dimension (:), intent ( in ) :: x !! halo's scaled variables real ( wp ), dimension (:), intent ( out ) :: g !! the Jacobian's nonzeros real ( wp ), dimension (:), allocatable :: jac , ks , jr integer , dimension (:), allocatable :: first_nz integer :: k , j , o , i logical :: ok select type ( me ) type is ( eclipse_newton_type ) call me % d % mission % compute_jacobian_stm ( x , jac ) ! (also puts x in the segments) g ( 1 : me % d % nnz_halo ) = jac allocate ( ks ( size ( me % d % rows )), jr ( sum ( me % d % rows % ncol )), first_nz ( size ( me % d % rows ))) o = 0 do k = 1 , size ( me % d % rows ) first_nz ( k ) = o o = o + me % d % rows ( k )% ncol end do call eval_rows ( me % d , ks , jr , ok = ok , only = me % mask ) j = me % d % nnz_halo do k = 1 , size ( me % active ) i = me % active ( k ) g ( j + 1 : j + me % d % rows ( i )% ncol ) = jr ( first_nz ( i ) + 1 : first_nz ( i ) + me % d % rows ( i )% ncol ) j = j + me % d % rows ( i )% ncol end do class default error stop 'newton_grad: invalid class' end select end subroutine newton_grad !***************************************************************************************** !***************************************************************************************** !> !  The Newton finish's iteration printout. subroutine newton_export ( me , x , f , iter ) class ( nlesolver_type ), intent ( inout ) :: me real ( wp ), dimension (:), intent ( in ) :: x !! the variables real ( wp ), dimension (:), intent ( in ) :: f !! the functions integer , intent ( in ) :: iter !! the iteration integer :: m select type ( me ) type is ( eclipse_newton_type ) m = me % d % m_halo if ( size ( f ) > m ) then write ( * , '(A,I4,A,ES12.4,A,ES12.4)' ) '     iter ' , iter , ': continuity norm ' , norm2 ( f ( 1 : m )), & ', eclipse rows max |KS - phi_min| ' , maxval ( abs ( f ( m + 1 :))) else write ( * , '(A,I4,A,ES12.4)' ) '     iter ' , iter , ': continuity norm ' , norm2 ( f ( 1 : m )) end if class default error stop 'newton_export: invalid class' end select end subroutine newton_export !***************************************************************************************** !***************************************************************************************** !> !  Equilibrate the continuity Jacobian at `x` for the optimization (`eclipse_opt_equilibrate`): !  alternately normalize its rows (weights `w`) and its columns (the variables' factors `r`, !  the optimization's variables being `x/r`), a few times, so that the rows and the columns !  all have 2-norms near 1. This lowers the condition number of the KKT systems of sqpopt's !  QP subproblems (for 100 revolutions, J's condition number goes from 8e4 to 7e2). The !  objective, `|x/r - x0/r|&#94;2/2`, is then measured in these units. subroutine equilibrate ( d , x ) type ( eclipse_opt_data ), intent ( inout ) :: d real ( wp ), dimension (:), intent ( in ) :: x real ( wp ), dimension (:), allocatable :: jac , a , norms integer :: it , k call d % mission % compute_jacobian_stm ( x , jac ) allocate ( a ( size ( jac )), norms ( max ( size ( d % r ), size ( d % w )))) d % r = one d % w = one do it = 1 , 10 a = jac * d % r ( d % icol ) * d % w ( d % irow ) norms = zero do k = 1 , size ( a ) norms ( d % irow ( k )) = norms ( d % irow ( k )) + a ( k ) ** 2 end do where ( norms ( 1 : size ( d % w )) > zero ) d % w = d % w / sqrt ( norms ( 1 : size ( d % w ))) a = jac * d % r ( d % icol ) * d % w ( d % irow ) norms = zero do k = 1 , size ( a ) norms ( d % icol ( k )) = norms ( d % icol ( k )) + a ( k ) ** 2 end do where ( norms ( 1 : size ( d % r )) > zero ) d % r = d % r / sqrt ( norms ( 1 : size ( d % r ))) end do write ( * , '(A,2ES10.2,A,2ES10.2)' ) '   equilibrated: column factors ' , minval ( d % r ), maxval ( d % r ), & ', row weights ' , minval ( d % w ), maxval ( d % w ) end subroutine equilibrate !***************************************************************************************** !***************************************************************************************** !> !  The largest change of each of the optimization's variables in one sqpopt iteration !  (`problem%set_max_step`), from the limits in physical units (`eclipse_opt_max_step_*`): !  a variable's unscaled value is `y*r*xscale` (plus its offset), so its limit is !  `limit/(r*xscale)`. A variable without a limit gets `sqpopt_infinity`. function step_limits ( d ) result ( lim ) type ( eclipse_opt_data ), intent ( in ) :: d real ( wp ), dimension (:), allocatable :: lim !! (allocatable: sized by the problem, so not on the stack) integer :: i , k , n_full , cc integer , dimension (:), allocatable :: removed real ( wp ) :: phys call d % mission % define_problem_size ( n = n_full , full_problem = . true .) removed = d % mission % removed_columns () allocate ( lim ( size ( d % r ))) lim = sqpopt_infinity k = 0 do i = 1 , n_full if ( any ( removed == i )) cycle k = k + 1 cc = mod ( i - 1 , 7 ) + 1 select case ( cc ) case ( 1 ); phys = d % mission % eclipse_opt_max_step_epoch case ( 2 : 4 ); phys = d % mission % eclipse_opt_max_step_position case default ; phys = d % mission % eclipse_opt_max_step_velocity end select if ( phys > zero ) lim ( k ) = phys / ( d % r ( k ) * d % mission % xscale ( k )) end do end function step_limits !***************************************************************************************** !***************************************************************************************** !> !  If all the node epochs of `x` (halo's scaled variables) are within the range of the !  splined ephemeris (2 periods before the reference epoch to 2 periods after the last rev, !  see [[initialize_the_mission]]), less a margin of half a period. A trial point of the !  optimization can be far off. function epochs_in_range ( d , x ) result ( ok ) type ( eclipse_opt_data ), intent ( in ) :: d real ( wp ), dimension (:), intent ( in ) :: x logical :: ok real ( wp ) :: lo , hi , t integer :: i lo = - 1.5_wp * d % mission % period hi = ( d % mission % n_revs + 1.5_wp ) * d % mission % period ok = . true . do i = 1 , size ( x ) if (. not . d % mission % x_is_epoch ( i )) cycle t = x ( i ) * d % mission % xscale ( i ) + d % mission % xoffset ( i ) ! [days from the reference epoch] if ( t < lo . or . t > hi . or . t /= t ) then ok = . false . return end if end do end function epochs_in_range !***************************************************************************************** !***************************************************************************************** !> !  The KS aggregate of values `ks`:  k_{lo} - \\frac{1}{\\rho} \\ln \\sum_k e&#94;{-\\rho (k_k - k_{lo})} . !  Of the segments' KS rows, it is exactly the KS of all their samples. pure function ks_aggregate ( ks , rho ) result ( agg ) real ( wp ), dimension (:), intent ( in ) :: ks real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: rho real ( wp ) :: agg real ( wp ) :: kmin kmin = minval ( ks ) agg = kmin - log ( sum ( exp ( - rho * ( ks - kmin )))) / rho end function ks_aggregate !***************************************************************************************** !***************************************************************************************** !> !  With `single`: the columns of the single eclipse row (the union of the segment rows'), !  and where each segment row's column is in them. subroutine union_columns ( d ) type ( eclipse_opt_data ), intent ( inout ) :: d integer :: k , j , o , i , nu if ( allocated ( d % ucol )) deallocate ( d % ucol ) if ( allocated ( d % upos )) deallocate ( d % upos ) allocate ( d % ucol ( sum ( d % rows % ncol )), d % upos ( sum ( d % rows % ncol ))) nu = 0 o = 0 do k = 1 , size ( d % rows ) do j = 1 , d % rows ( k )% ncol i = findloc ( d % ucol ( 1 : nu ), d % rows ( k )% col ( j ), 1 ) if ( i == 0 ) then nu = nu + 1 d % ucol ( nu ) = d % rows ( k )% col ( j ) i = nu end if d % upos ( o + j ) = i end do o = o + d % rows ( k )% ncol end do d % ucol = d % ucol ( 1 : nu ) end subroutine union_columns !***************************************************************************************** !***************************************************************************************** !> !  Multiply the eclipse rows' partials by the optimization's variable scaling `r`. subroutine scale_row_columns ( d , jac ) type ( eclipse_opt_data ), intent ( in ) :: d real ( wp ), dimension (:), intent ( inout ) :: jac integer :: k , j , o o = 0 do k = 1 , size ( d % rows ) do j = 1 , d % rows ( k )% ncol jac ( o + j ) = jac ( o + j ) * d % r ( d % rows ( k )% col ( j )) end do o = o + d % rows ( k )% ncol end do end subroutine scale_row_columns !***************************************************************************************** !***************************************************************************************** !> !  The KS aggregate of the shadow function at a row's samples, for the given start epoch, !  final epoch [days] and initial rotating-frame state (a copy of the segment is propagated, !  with output every `eclipse_opt_sample_step` seconds). function row_ks ( mission , seg , row , t0 , tf , x0_rotating , ok ) result ( ks ) class ( mission_type ), intent ( in ) :: mission type ( segment ), intent ( in ) :: seg type ( eclipse_row ), intent ( in ) :: row real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: t0 , tf real ( wp ), dimension ( 6 ), intent ( in ) :: x0_rotating logical , intent ( out ) :: ok !! false if the segment has none of the row's samples (e.g., a trial point !! that moved its epochs far): the row can't be evaluated there real ( wp ) :: ks type ( segment ) :: s real ( wp ), dimension (:), allocatable :: phi real ( wp ), dimension ( 6 ) :: rv real ( wp ) :: step , rho , pmin integer :: i , k , n , np step = mission % eclipse_opt_sample_step rho = mission % eclipse_opt_ks_rho s = seg call s % traj_inertial % destroy () call s % traj_rotating % destroy () call s % traj_se_rotating % destroy () call s % set_input ( t0 , tf , x0_rotating ) call s % propagate ( mode = 2 , tstep = step ) if ( s % failed ) then ok = . false . ks = zero return end if ! the samples: the points at k*step from the start (the last point, at tf, is only one ! of them if it falls on the grid) n = size ( s % traj_inertial % et ) allocate ( phi ( row % k_hi - row % k_lo + 1 )) np = 0 do k = row % k_lo , row % k_hi i = k + 1 if ( i > n ) exit if ( abs ( abs ( s % traj_inertial % et ( i ) - s % traj_inertial % et ( 1 )) - k * step ) > 1.0e-3_wp ) exit rv = [ s % traj_inertial % x ( i ), s % traj_inertial % y ( i ), s % traj_inertial % z ( i ), & s % traj_inertial % vx ( i ), s % traj_inertial % vy ( i ), s % traj_inertial % vz ( i )] np = np + 1 phi ( np ) = get_sun_fraction ( s % eph , s % traj_inertial % et ( i ), rv , mission % eclipse_opt_bubble ) end do ok = np > 0 if (. not . ok ) then ks = zero return end if pmin = minval ( phi ( 1 : np )) ks = pmin - log ( sum ( exp ( - rho * ( phi ( 1 : np ) - pmin )))) / rho end function row_ks !***************************************************************************************** !***************************************************************************************** !> !  Check the shadow function along the whole trajectory (every `eclipse_opt_detect_step` !  seconds), and make the rows of the segments that come near the shadow (where the shadow !  function, with the constraints' bubble, is below `eclipse_opt_detect_phi`). subroutine find_rows ( mission , x , rows , phimin , shadow_min ) class ( mission_type ), intent ( inout ) :: mission real ( wp ), dimension (:), intent ( in ) :: x type ( eclipse_row ), dimension (:), allocatable , intent ( out ) :: rows real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: phimin !! the smallest shadow function (no bubble) along the trajectory real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: shadow_min !! the time in the shadow [min] (approximate: the number of points !! in the shadow times the step) integer :: n_segs , iseg , i , n , n_full , nk , kmax , nr real ( wp ), dimension (:), allocatable :: seg_phimin , seg_lo , seg_hi integer , dimension (:), allocatable :: seg_nshadow , full2red , removed logical , dimension (:), allocatable :: seg_near real ( wp ) :: dt , phi0 , phib , step real ( wp ), dimension ( 6 ) :: rv call mission % define_problem_size ( n_segs = n_segs ) call mission % define_problem_size ( n = n_full , full_problem = . true .) call mission % put_x_in_segments ( x ) allocate ( seg_phimin ( n_segs ), seg_lo ( n_segs ), seg_hi ( n_segs ), seg_nshadow ( n_segs ), seg_near ( n_segs )) seg_phimin = huge ( one ); seg_lo = huge ( one ); seg_hi = - huge ( one ); seg_nshadow = 0 ; seg_near = . false . !$OMP PARALLEL DO PRIVATE(iseg,i,n,dt,phi0,phib,rv) SCHEDULE(dynamic) do iseg = 1 , n_segs associate ( seg => mission % segs ( iseg )) call seg % traj_inertial % destroy () call seg % traj_rotating % destroy () call seg % traj_se_rotating % destroy () call seg % propagate ( mode = 2 , tstep = mission % eclipse_opt_detect_step ) n = size ( seg % traj_inertial % et ) do i = 1 , n rv = [ seg % traj_inertial % x ( i ), seg % traj_inertial % y ( i ), seg % traj_inertial % z ( i ), & seg % traj_inertial % vx ( i ), seg % traj_inertial % vy ( i ), seg % traj_inertial % vz ( i )] phi0 = get_sun_fraction ( seg % eph , seg % traj_inertial % et ( i ), rv , zero ) if ( mission % eclipse_opt_bubble > zero ) then phib = get_sun_fraction ( seg % eph , seg % traj_inertial % et ( i ), rv , mission % eclipse_opt_bubble ) else phib = phi0 end if seg_phimin ( iseg ) = min ( seg_phimin ( iseg ), phi0 ) if ( phi0 < zero ) seg_nshadow ( iseg ) = seg_nshadow ( iseg ) + 1 if ( phib < mission % eclipse_opt_detect_phi ) then dt = abs ( seg % traj_inertial % et ( i ) - seg % traj_inertial % et ( 1 )) ! [sec from the start] seg_near ( iseg ) = . true . seg_lo ( iseg ) = min ( seg_lo ( iseg ), dt ) seg_hi ( iseg ) = max ( seg_hi ( iseg ), dt ) end if end do call seg % traj_inertial % destroy () call seg % traj_rotating % destroy () call seg % traj_se_rotating % destroy () end associate end do !$OMP END PARALLEL DO phimin = minval ( seg_phimin ) shadow_min = real ( sum ( seg_nshadow ), wp ) * mission % eclipse_opt_detect_step / 6 0.0_wp ! the map from the full problem's columns to x: removed = mission % removed_columns () allocate ( full2red ( n_full )) full2red = 0 nk = 0 do i = 1 , n_full if ( any ( removed == i )) cycle nk = nk + 1 full2red ( i ) = nk end do ! the rows: the samples across the near-shadow part of each flagged segment, padded by one ! sample on each side (and not past the segment's last full step) step = mission % eclipse_opt_sample_step allocate ( rows ( count ( seg_near ))) nr = 0 do iseg = 1 , n_segs if (. not . seg_near ( iseg )) cycle associate ( seg => mission % segs ( iseg )) kmax = floor ( abs ( seg % data % tf - seg % data % t0 ) * day2sec / step - 1.0e-6_wp ) nr = nr + 1 rows ( nr )% iseg = iseg rows ( nr )% k_lo = max ( 0 , floor ( seg_lo ( iseg ) / step ) - 1 ) rows ( nr )% k_hi = min ( kmax , ceiling ( seg_hi ( iseg ) / step ) + 1 ) call row_columns ( iseg , full2red , rows ( nr )) end associate end do end subroutine find_rows !***************************************************************************************** !***************************************************************************************** !> !  The variables a row of segment `iseg` depends on: the epoch and state of its start node. subroutine row_columns ( iseg , full2red , row ) integer , intent ( in ) :: iseg integer , dimension (:), intent ( in ) :: full2red type ( eclipse_row ), intent ( inout ) :: row integer :: irev , l , js , ks , k , fc irev = ( iseg - 1 ) / 8 l = iseg - 8 * irev js = 4 * irev + start_node ( l ) ks = 4 * irev + tf_node ( l ) row % tf_with_t0 = ks == js row % ncol = 0 do k = 1 , 7 fc = 7 * ( js - 1 ) + k if ( full2red ( fc ) > 0 ) then row % ncol = row % ncol + 1 row % col ( row % ncol ) = full2red ( fc ) row % kind ( row % ncol ) = k - 1 end if end do end subroutine row_columns !***************************************************************************************** !***************************************************************************************** !> !  Add the new rows: a segment already in the list gets the union of the sample ranges. subroutine merge_rows ( rows , new ) type ( eclipse_row ), dimension (:), allocatable , intent ( inout ) :: rows type ( eclipse_row ), dimension (:), intent ( in ) :: new integer :: k , j logical :: found do k = 1 , size ( new ) found = . false . do j = 1 , size ( rows ) if ( rows ( j )% iseg == new ( k )% iseg ) then rows ( j )% k_lo = min ( rows ( j )% k_lo , new ( k )% k_lo ) rows ( j )% k_hi = max ( rows ( j )% k_hi , new ( k )% k_hi ) found = . true . exit end if end do if (. not . found ) rows = [ rows , new ( k )] end do end subroutine merge_rows !***************************************************************************************** !***************************************************************************************** !> !  Print how far the optimization moved the solution. subroutine report_change ( mission , x0 , x ) class ( mission_type ), intent ( inout ) :: mission real ( wp ), dimension (:), intent ( in ) :: x0 , x integer :: i , n_full , k , cc integer , dimension (:), allocatable :: removed real ( wp ) :: dt_max , dr_max , dv_max , d call mission % define_problem_size ( n = n_full , full_problem = . true .) removed = mission % removed_columns () dt_max = zero ; dr_max = zero ; dv_max = zero k = 0 do i = 1 , n_full if ( any ( removed == i )) cycle k = k + 1 d = abs ( x ( k ) - x0 ( k )) * mission % xscale ( k ) ! unscaled cc = mod ( i - 1 , 7 ) + 1 select case ( cc ) case ( 1 ); dt_max = max ( dt_max , d ) case ( 2 : 4 ); dr_max = max ( dr_max , d ) case ( 5 : 7 ); dv_max = max ( dv_max , d ) end select end do write ( * , '(A,F10.3,A,F12.3,A,F10.3,A)' ) '   largest change of a node: ' , dt_max * 2 4.0_wp , ' h in epoch, ' , & dr_max , ' km in position, ' , dv_max * 100 0.0_wp , ' m/s in velocity' end subroutine report_change !***************************************************************************************** end submodule halo_eclipse_opt_submodule !*****************************************************************************************","tags":"","url":"sourcefile/halo_eclipse_opt_submodule.f90.html"},{"title":"splined_ephemeris_module.f90 – halo","text":"This file depends on sourcefile~~splined_ephemeris_module.f90~~EfferentGraph sourcefile~splined_ephemeris_module.f90 splined_ephemeris_module.f90 sourcefile~halo_kinds_module.f90 halo_kinds_module.F90 sourcefile~splined_ephemeris_module.f90->sourcefile~halo_kinds_module.f90 Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Source File Source File This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a file to a file which it depends on. A file\nis dependent upon another if the latter must be compiled before the former\ncan be. Files dependent on this one sourcefile~~splined_ephemeris_module.f90~~AfferentGraph sourcefile~splined_ephemeris_module.f90 splined_ephemeris_module.f90 sourcefile~halo_module.f90 halo_module.F90 sourcefile~halo_module.f90->sourcefile~splined_ephemeris_module.f90 sourcefile~halo_utilities_module.f90 halo_utilities_module.f90 sourcefile~halo_module.f90->sourcefile~halo_utilities_module.f90 sourcefile~halo_utilities_module.f90->sourcefile~splined_ephemeris_module.f90 sourcefile~halo_eclipse_opt_submodule.f90 halo_eclipse_opt_submodule.F90 sourcefile~halo_eclipse_opt_submodule.f90->sourcefile~halo_module.f90 Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Source File Source File This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a file to a file which it depends on. A file\nis dependent upon another if the latter must be compiled before the former\ncan be. Source Code !***************************************************************************************** !> !  Simple splined ephemeris model for Earth/Sun wrt Moon. module splined_ephemeris_module use fortran_astrodynamics_toolkit use bspline_module , only : db1ink , db1val , bspline_order_cubic use iso_fortran_env use halo_kinds_module implicit none private ! spline parameters: integer , parameter :: kx = bspline_order_cubic !! spline interpolation order integer , parameter :: iknot = 0 !! use default knots ! the coefficients are stored as global variables, ! so all the segments can access them without having ! to have multiple copies of the ephemeris in each segment type :: body_eph integer :: id = 0 real ( wp ), dimension (:,:), allocatable :: f !! function evals. not needed once the spline has been computed real ( wp ), dimension (:,:), allocatable :: tx real ( wp ), dimension (:,:), allocatable :: bcoef integer :: nx = 0 contains procedure , public :: destroy => destroy_body_eph procedure , public :: allocate => allocate_body_eph procedure , public :: populate => populate_body_eph procedure , public :: spline => spline_body_eph end type body_eph type ( body_eph ), target :: earth_eph type ( body_eph ), target :: sun_eph type ( body_eph ), target :: ssb_eph type ( body_eph ), target :: jupiter_eph type :: body_eph_interface !! the interface to a splined ephemeris for a body !! used for calls to `db1val`. private integer :: inbvx = 0 real ( wp ), dimension (:), allocatable :: w0 !! work array - dimension(3_ip*kx) type ( body_eph ), pointer :: eph => null () !! points to the ephemeris contains procedure , public :: get_r procedure , public :: get_rv procedure , public :: get_rv_dot procedure , public :: destroy => destroy_body_eph_interface procedure , public :: initialize => initialize_body_eph_interface end type body_eph_interface type , extends ( jpl_ephemeris ), public :: jpl_ephemeris_splined !! make this an extension of the [[jpl_ephemeris]], !! since it is also needed in tranformations. type ( body_eph_interface ) :: earth_eph_interface !! splined version of earth ephemeris type ( body_eph_interface ) :: sun_eph_interface !! splined version of sun ephemeris type ( body_eph_interface ) :: ssb_eph_interface !! splined version of ssb ephemeris type ( body_eph_interface ) :: jupiter_eph_interface !! splined version of jupiter ephemeris contains procedure , public :: initialize_splinded_ephemeris procedure :: initialize_globals !! this is done once to initialize the global ephemeris vars procedure , public :: get_r => get_r_splined procedure , public :: get_rv => get_rv_splined procedure , public :: get_rv_derivative => get_rv_derivative_splined procedure , public :: destroy => destroy_jpl_ephemeris_splined end type jpl_ephemeris_splined contains subroutine destroy_jpl_ephemeris_splined ( me ) class ( jpl_ephemeris_splined ), intent ( inout ) :: me call me % earth_eph_interface % destroy () call me % sun_eph_interface % destroy () call me % ssb_eph_interface % destroy () call me % jupiter_eph_interface % destroy () end subroutine destroy_jpl_ephemeris_splined subroutine destroy_body_eph ( me ) class ( body_eph ), intent ( out ) :: me end subroutine destroy_body_eph subroutine allocate_body_eph ( me , nx , kx ) class ( body_eph ), intent ( inout ) :: me integer , intent ( in ) :: nx integer , intent ( in ) :: kx me % nx = nx allocate ( me % tx ( nx + kx , 6 )) ! columns are for each state element (rx,ry,rz,vx,vy,vz) allocate ( me % bcoef ( nx , 6 )) allocate ( me % f ( nx , 6 )) end subroutine allocate_body_eph subroutine populate_body_eph ( me , eph , et , targ , obs , i ) !! populate the `f` array with the ephemeris data class ( body_eph ), intent ( inout ) :: me type ( jpl_ephemeris ), intent ( inout ) :: eph real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: et !! ephemeris time [sec] type ( celestial_body ), intent ( in ) :: targ !! target body type ( celestial_body ), intent ( in ) :: obs !! observer body integer , intent ( in ) :: i !! index in the ephemeris logical :: status_ok call eph % get_rv ( et , targ , obs , me % f ( i ,:), status_ok ) if (. not . status_ok ) error stop 'eph error' end subroutine populate_body_eph subroutine spline_body_eph ( me , et_vec , i ) class ( body_eph ), intent ( inout ) :: me real ( wp ), dimension (:), intent ( in ) :: et_vec !! ephemeris time vector [sec] integer , intent ( in ) :: i !! state element index (1-6) integer :: iflag call db1ink ( et_vec , me % nx , me % f (:, i ), kx , iknot , me % tx (:, i ), me % bcoef (:, i ), iflag ) if ( iflag /= 0 ) then write ( * , * ) 'db1ink iflag = ' , iflag error stop 'db1ink error' end if end subroutine spline_body_eph subroutine destroy_body_eph_interface ( me ) class ( body_eph_interface ), intent ( inout ) :: me if ( associated ( me % eph )) call me % eph % destroy () me % eph => null () if ( allocated ( me % w0 )) deallocate ( me % w0 ) me % inbvx = 0 end subroutine destroy_body_eph_interface subroutine initialize_body_eph_interface ( me , eph ) class ( body_eph_interface ), intent ( inout ) :: me type ( body_eph ), target :: eph allocate ( me % w0 ( 3 * kx )) me % inbvx = 0 me % eph => eph ! point to the global ephemeris end subroutine initialize_body_eph_interface subroutine initialize_globals ( me , et0 , dt , etf ) !! initialize the earth and sun ephemeris. class ( jpl_ephemeris_splined ), intent ( inout ) :: me real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: et0 !! initial ephemeris time [sec] real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: dt !! ephemeris time step [sec] real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: etf !! final ephemeris time [sec] integer :: i !! counter real ( wp ) :: et !! ephemeris time integer :: nx !! number of points real ( wp ), dimension (:), allocatable :: et_vec integer :: iflag ! write(*,*) 'initialize_globals...' ! write(*,*) '  et0 = ', et0 ! write(*,*) '  dt  = ', dt ! write(*,*) '  etf = ', etf call me % destroy () call earth_eph % destroy () call sun_eph % destroy () call ssb_eph % destroy () call jupiter_eph % destroy () ! first, count the number of points and allocate the arrays: nx = 0 et = et0 do if ( et > etf ) exit nx = nx + 1 et = et + dt end do call earth_eph % allocate ( nx , kx ) call sun_eph % allocate ( nx , kx ) call ssb_eph % allocate ( nx , kx ) call jupiter_eph % allocate ( nx , kx ) allocate ( et_vec ( nx )) ! function calls from et0 to etf: i = 0 ! index in the arrays et = et0 do if ( et > etf ) exit i = i + 1 et = et + dt et_vec ( i ) = et call earth_eph % populate ( me % jpl_ephemeris , et , body_earth , body_moon , i ) call sun_eph % populate ( me % jpl_ephemeris , et , body_sun , body_moon , i ) call ssb_eph % populate ( me % jpl_ephemeris , et , body_ssb , body_moon , i ) call jupiter_eph % populate ( me % jpl_ephemeris , et , body_jupiter , body_moon , i ) end do ! create the splines (one for each coordinate): do i = 1 , 6 call earth_eph % spline ( et_vec , i ) call sun_eph % spline ( et_vec , i ) call ssb_eph % spline ( et_vec , i ) call jupiter_eph % spline ( et_vec , i ) end do deallocate ( earth_eph % f ) ! don't need these anymore deallocate ( sun_eph % f ) deallocate ( ssb_eph % f ) deallocate ( jupiter_eph % f ) end subroutine initialize_globals subroutine initialize_splinded_ephemeris ( me , filename , ksize , km , bary , status_ok , et0 , dt , etf ) !! the ephemeris must be initialized before this is called class ( jpl_ephemeris_splined ), intent ( inout ) :: me character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: filename !! ephemeris file name integer , intent ( in ), optional :: ksize !! corresponding `ksize` logical , intent ( in ), optional :: km !! defining physical units of the output states. !! `km = .true.`  : km and km/sec [default], !! `km = .false.` : au and au/day. logical , intent ( in ), optional :: bary !! logical flag defining output center. !! only the 9 planets are affected. !! `bary = .true.`  : center is solar-system barycenter, !! `bary = .false.` : center is sun [default]. logical , intent ( out ) :: status_ok !! true if there were no problems. real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: et0 !! initial ephemeris time [sec] real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: dt !! ephemeris time step [sec] real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: etf !! final ephemeris time [sec] write ( * , '(A)' ) ' * Using splined ephemeris' ! have to first initialize the base one: call me % jpl_ephemeris % initialize ( filename , ksize , km , bary , status_ok ) status_ok = ( etf > et0 . and . dt > 0.0_wp ) if (. not . status_ok ) return ! initialize the global spline coefficients call me % initialize_globals ( et0 , abs ( dt ), etf ) ! now, the local variables in this class call me % earth_eph_interface % initialize ( earth_eph ) call me % sun_eph_interface % initialize ( sun_eph ) call me % ssb_eph_interface % initialize ( ssb_eph ) call me % jupiter_eph_interface % initialize ( jupiter_eph ) end subroutine initialize_splinded_ephemeris subroutine get_rv_splined ( me , et , targ , obs , rv , status_ok ) class ( jpl_ephemeris_splined ), intent ( inout ) :: me real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: et !! ephemeris time [sec] type ( celestial_body ), intent ( in ) :: targ !! target body type ( celestial_body ), intent ( in ) :: obs !! observer body real ( wp ), dimension ( 6 ), intent ( out ) :: rv !! state of targ w.r.t. obs [km,km/s] in ICRF frame logical , intent ( out ) :: status_ok !! true if there were no problems status_ok = . true . if ( targ == body_earth . and . obs == body_moon ) then rv = me % earth_eph_interface % get_rv ( et ) elseif ( targ == body_sun . and . obs == body_moon ) then rv = me % sun_eph_interface % get_rv ( et ) elseif ( targ == body_ssb . and . obs == body_moon ) then rv = me % ssb_eph_interface % get_rv ( et ) elseif ( targ == body_jupiter . and . obs == body_moon ) then rv = me % jupiter_eph_interface % get_rv ( et ) elseif ( targ == body_moon . and . obs == body_earth ) then ! inverse are negative rv = - me % earth_eph_interface % get_rv ( et ) elseif ( targ == body_moon . and . obs == body_sun ) then rv = - me % sun_eph_interface % get_rv ( et ) elseif ( targ == body_moon . and . obs == body_ssb ) then rv = - me % ssb_eph_interface % get_rv ( et ) elseif ( targ == body_moon . and . obs == body_jupiter ) then rv = - me % jupiter_eph_interface % get_rv ( et ) elseif ( targ == body_earth . and . obs == body_sun ) then ! for this one we subtract these rv = me % earth_eph_interface % get_rv ( et ) - me % sun_eph_interface % get_rv ( et ) else write ( * , * ) 'targ = ' , targ write ( * , * ) 'obs  = ' , obs error stop 'error in get_rv_splined: this combo has not been splined' ! or could call me%jpl_ephemeris%get_rv(et,targ,obs,rv,status_ok) end if end subroutine get_rv_splined subroutine get_rv_derivative_splined ( me , et , targ , obs , rvdot , status_ok ) !! The time derivative of the splined state returned by [[get_rv_splined]] !! (the derivative of each component's spline: so `rvdot(1:3)` is the derivative of !! the position spline, which is close to, but not exactly, the velocity spline). !! Only the Earth/Moon pairs are available. class ( jpl_ephemeris_splined ), intent ( inout ) :: me real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: et !! ephemeris time [sec] type ( celestial_body ), intent ( in ) :: targ !! target body type ( celestial_body ), intent ( in ) :: obs !! observer body real ( wp ), dimension ( 6 ), intent ( out ) :: rvdot !! d/dt of the state of targ w.r.t. obs [km/s, km/s&#94;2] logical , intent ( out ) :: status_ok !! true if there were no problems status_ok = . true . if ( targ == body_earth . and . obs == body_moon ) then rvdot = me % earth_eph_interface % get_rv_dot ( et ) elseif ( targ == body_moon . and . obs == body_earth ) then rvdot = - me % earth_eph_interface % get_rv_dot ( et ) else write ( * , * ) 'targ = ' , targ write ( * , * ) 'obs  = ' , obs error stop 'error in get_rv_derivative_splined: this combo is not available' end if end subroutine get_rv_derivative_splined subroutine get_r_splined ( me , et , targ , obs , r , status_ok ) class ( jpl_ephemeris_splined ), intent ( inout ) :: me real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: et !! ephemeris time [sec] type ( celestial_body ), intent ( in ) :: targ !! target body type ( celestial_body ), intent ( in ) :: obs !! observer body real ( wp ), dimension ( 3 ), intent ( out ) :: r !! r of targ w.r.t. obs [km] in ICRF frame logical , intent ( out ) :: status_ok !! true if there were no problems status_ok = . true . if ( targ == body_earth . and . obs == body_moon ) then r = me % earth_eph_interface % get_r ( et ) elseif ( targ == body_sun . and . obs == body_moon ) then r = me % sun_eph_interface % get_r ( et ) elseif ( targ == body_ssb . and . obs == body_moon ) then r = me % ssb_eph_interface % get_r ( et ) elseif ( targ == body_jupiter . and . obs == body_moon ) then r = me % jupiter_eph_interface % get_r ( et ) elseif ( targ == body_moon . and . obs == body_earth ) then ! inverse are negative r = - me % earth_eph_interface % get_r ( et ) elseif ( targ == body_moon . and . obs == body_sun ) then r = - me % sun_eph_interface % get_r ( et ) elseif ( targ == body_moon . and . obs == body_ssb ) then r = - me % ssb_eph_interface % get_r ( et ) elseif ( targ == body_moon . and . obs == body_jupiter ) then r = - me % jupiter_eph_interface % get_r ( et ) elseif ( targ == body_sun . and . obs == body_ssb ) then ! for this one we subtract these ! ssb -> sun = ssb -> moon + moon -> sun r = me % sun_eph_interface % get_r ( et ) - me % ssb_eph_interface % get_r ( et ) elseif ( targ == body_earth . and . obs == body_ssb ) then ! for this one we subtract these ! ssb -> earth = ssb -> moon + moon -> earth r = me % earth_eph_interface % get_r ( et ) - me % ssb_eph_interface % get_r ( et ) else write ( * , * ) 'targ = ' , targ write ( * , * ) 'obs  = ' , obs error stop 'error in get_r_splined: this combo has not been splined' ! or could call me%jpl_ephemeris%get_rv(et,targ,obs,rv,status_ok); r = rv(1:3) end if end subroutine get_r_splined function get_rv ( me , et ) result ( rv ) class ( body_eph_interface ), intent ( inout ) :: me real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: et !! ephemeris time (sec) real ( wp ), dimension ( 6 ) :: rv !! position/velocity vector integer :: iflag , i do i = 1 , 6 call db1val ( et , 0 , me % eph % tx (:, i ), me % eph % nx , kx , me % eph % bcoef (:, i ), rv ( i ), iflag , & me % inbvx , me % w0 , extrap = . false .) if ( iflag /= 0 ) then write ( * , * ) 'et    = ' , et write ( * , * ) 'iflag = ' , iflag error stop 'error calling get_rv' end if end do end function get_rv function get_rv_dot ( me , et ) result ( rvdot ) !! time derivative of each component's spline class ( body_eph_interface ), intent ( inout ) :: me real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: et !! ephemeris time (sec) real ( wp ), dimension ( 6 ) :: rvdot !! d/dt of the position/velocity vector integer :: iflag , i do i = 1 , 6 call db1val ( et , 1 , me % eph % tx (:, i ), me % eph % nx , kx , me % eph % bcoef (:, i ), rvdot ( i ), iflag , & me % inbvx , me % w0 , extrap = . false .) if ( iflag /= 0 ) then write ( * , * ) 'et    = ' , et write ( * , * ) 'iflag = ' , iflag error stop 'error calling get_rv_dot' end if end do end function get_rv_dot function get_r ( me , et ) result ( r ) class ( body_eph_interface ), intent ( inout ) :: me real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: et !! ephemeris time (sec) real ( wp ), dimension ( 3 ) :: r !! position vector integer :: iflag , i do i = 1 , 3 call db1val ( et , 0 , me % eph % tx (:, i ), me % eph % nx , kx , me % eph % bcoef (:, i ), r ( i ), iflag , & me % inbvx , me % w0 , extrap = . false .) if ( iflag /= 0 ) then write ( * , * ) 'iflag = ' , iflag error stop 'error calling get_r' end if end do end function get_r ! notes: ! ! can we also spline the frame. ! maybe as a quaternion? ! ! use M2Q to convert matrix to quaternion -> interpolate -> Q2M to convert back to matrix ! ! Interpolates between two 3x3 rotation matrices R1 and R2 by fraction t (0 <= t <= 1) ! ! Uses quaternion SLERP for smooth interpolation. ! function interpolate_rotation_matrix(R1, R2, t) result(Rout) !     use, intrinsic :: iso_fortran_env, only: wp => real64 !     implicit none !     real(wp), intent(in) :: R1(3,3), R2(3,3) !     real(wp), intent(in) :: t !     real(wp) :: Rout(3,3) !     real(wp) :: q1(4), q2(4), q_interp(4) !     ! Convert rotation matrices to quaternions !     call rotmat_to_quat(R1, q1) !     call rotmat_to_quat(R2, q2) !     ! Spherical linear interpolation (SLERP) between quaternions !     call slerp_quat(q1, q2, t, q_interp) !     ! Convert interpolated quaternion back to rotation matrix !     call quat_to_rotmat(q_interp, Rout) ! end function interpolate_rotation_matrix ! ! Convert 3x3 rotation matrix to quaternion (w,x,y,z) ! subroutine rotmat_to_quat(R, q) !     real(wp), intent(in) :: R(3,3) !     real(wp), intent(out) :: q(4) !     real(wp) :: tr, S !     tr = R(1,1) + R(2,2) + R(3,3) !     if (tr > 0.0_wp) then !         S = sqrt(tr + 1.0_wp) * 2.0_wp !         q(1) = 0.25_wp * S !         q(2) = (R(3,2) - R(2,3)) / S !         q(3) = (R(1,3) - R(3,1)) / S !         q(4) = (R(2,1) - R(1,2)) / S !     else if ((R(1,1) > R(2,2)) .and. (R(1,1) > R(3,3))) then !         S = sqrt(1.0_wp + R(1,1) - R(2,2) - R(3,3)) * 2.0_wp !         q(1) = (R(3,2) - R(2,3)) / S !         q(2) = 0.25_wp * S !         q(3) = (R(1,2) + R(2,1)) / S !         q(4) = (R(1,3) + R(3,1)) / S !     else if (R(2,2) > R(3,3)) then !         S = sqrt(1.0_wp + R(2,2) - R(1,1) - R(3,3)) * 2.0_wp !         q(1) = (R(1,3) - R(3,1)) / S !         q(2) = (R(1,2) + R(2,1)) / S !         q(3) = 0.25_wp * S !         q(4) = (R(2,3) + R(3,2)) / S !     else !         S = sqrt(1.0_wp + R(3,3) - R(1,1) - R(2,2)) * 2.0_wp !         q(1) = (R(2,1) - R(1,2)) / S !         q(2) = (R(1,3) + R(3,1)) / S !         q(3) = (R(2,3) + R(3,2)) / S !         q(4) = 0.25_wp * S !     end if ! end subroutine rotmat_to_quat ! ! Spherical linear interpolation between two quaternions ! subroutine slerp_quat(q1, q2, t, qout) !     real(wp), intent(in) :: q1(4), q2(4) !     real(wp), intent(in) :: t !     real(wp), intent(out) :: qout(4) !     real(wp) :: cos_theta, theta, sin_theta, w1, w2 !     cos_theta = sum(q1 * q2) !     if (cos_theta < 0.0_wp) then !         cos_theta = -cos_theta !         q2 = -q2 !     end if !     if (cos_theta > 0.9995_wp) then !         qout = (1.0_wp - t) * q1 + t * q2 !         qout = qout / sqrt(sum(qout**2)) !         return !     end if !     theta = acos(cos_theta) !     sin_theta = sin(theta) !     w1 = sin((1.0_wp - t) * theta) / sin_theta !     w2 = sin(t * theta) / sin_theta !     qout = w1 * q1 + w2 * q2 ! end subroutine slerp_quat ! ! Convert quaternion (w,x,y,z) to 3x3 rotation matrix ! subroutine quat_to_rotmat(q, R) !     real(wp), intent(in) :: q(4) !     real(wp), intent(out) :: R(3,3) !     real(wp) :: w, x, y, z !     w = q(1); x = q(2); y = q(3); z = q(4) !     R(1,1) = 1.0_wp - 2.0_wp*(y*y + z*z) !     R(1,2) = 2.0_wp*(x*y - z*w) !     R(1,3) = 2.0_wp*(x*z + y*w) !     R(2,1) = 2.0_wp*(x*y + z*w) !     R(2,2) = 1.0_wp - 2.0_wp*(x*x + z*z) !     R(2,3) = 2.0_wp*(y*z - x*w) !     R(3,1) = 2.0_wp*(x*z - y*w) !     R(3,2) = 2.0_wp*(y*z + x*w) !     R(3,3) = 1.0_wp - 2.0_wp*(x*x + y*y) ! end subroutine quat_to_rotmat end module splined_ephemeris_module !*****************************************************************************************","tags":"","url":"sourcefile/splined_ephemeris_module.f90.html"},{"title":"parameters_module.f90 – halo","text":"This file depends on sourcefile~~parameters_module.f90~~EfferentGraph sourcefile~parameters_module.f90 parameters_module.f90 sourcefile~halo_kinds_module.f90 halo_kinds_module.F90 sourcefile~parameters_module.f90->sourcefile~halo_kinds_module.f90 Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Source File Source File This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a file to a file which it depends on. A file\nis dependent upon another if the latter must be compiled before the former\ncan be. Files dependent on this one sourcefile~~parameters_module.f90~~AfferentGraph sourcefile~parameters_module.f90 parameters_module.f90 sourcefile~config_file_module.f90 config_file_module.f90 sourcefile~config_file_module.f90->sourcefile~parameters_module.f90 sourcefile~halo_module.f90 halo_module.F90 sourcefile~halo_module.f90->sourcefile~parameters_module.f90 sourcefile~halo_module.f90->sourcefile~config_file_module.f90 sourcefile~halo_utilities_module.f90 halo_utilities_module.f90 sourcefile~halo_module.f90->sourcefile~halo_utilities_module.f90 sourcefile~halo_utilities_module.f90->sourcefile~parameters_module.f90 sourcefile~halo_eclipse_opt_submodule.f90 halo_eclipse_opt_submodule.F90 sourcefile~halo_eclipse_opt_submodule.f90->sourcefile~halo_module.f90 Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Source File Source File This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a file to a file which it depends on. A file\nis dependent upon another if the latter must be compiled before the former\ncan be. Source Code module parameters_module use halo_kinds_module , only : wp use fortran_astrodynamics_toolkit , only : zero implicit none private public :: wp ! real kind ! constants: integer , parameter , public :: n_eoms = 6 !! size of EOM derivative vector [x,y,z,vx,vy,vz] integer , parameter , public :: n_eoms_stm = n_eoms + n_eoms * n_eoms !! state and state transition matrix (42) real ( wp ), public :: mu_earth = 3.9860043543609593E+05_wp !!  \\mu_{earth}  real ( wp ), public :: mu_moon = 4.9028000661637961E+03_wp !!  \\mu_{moon}  real ( wp ), public :: mu_sun = 1.3271244004193938E+11_wp !!  \\mu_{sun}  real ( wp ), public :: mu_jupiter = 1.266865349218008E+08_wp !!  \\mu_{jupiter}  -- from https://naif.jpl.nasa.gov/pub/naif/generic_kernels/pck/gm_de431.tpc real ( wp ), public :: rad_moon = 173 7.4_wp !! radius of the Moon real ( wp ), public :: rad_sun = 69570 0.0_wp !! sun radius (km) real ( wp ), public :: rad_earth = 637 8.0_wp !! earth radius (km) integer , public :: maxnum = 10000 !! integrator max steps integer , public :: grav_n = 8 !! max grav degree integer , public :: grav_m = 8 !! max grav order integer , public :: grav_frame = 1 !! 1: iau_moon, 2: moon_pa (splined) real ( wp ), dimension (:), allocatable , public :: xscale_x0 ! scale values for opt vars [must be size 6] real ( wp ), dimension (:), allocatable , public :: fscale_xf ! scale values for constraints [must be size 6] real ( wp ), public :: fscale_rdot = 1.0_wp !! scale value for the rdot=0 constraint logical , public :: use_battin_gravity = . false . !! use Battin gravity formulation character ( len = :), allocatable , public :: mkspk_path !! for mkspk: path to mkspk executable. e.g. `kernel/mkspk` integer , public :: object_id = - 50000 !! for mkspk: OBJECT_ID character ( len = :), allocatable , public :: object_name !! for mkspk: OBJECT_NAME character ( len = :), allocatable , public :: leapseconds_file !! for mkspk: LEAPSECONDS_FILE character ( len = :), allocatable , public :: segment_id !! for mkspk: SEGMENT_ID integer , public :: polynom_degree = 9 !! for mkspk: POLYNOM_DEGREE integer , public :: output_spk_type = 9 !! for mkspk: OUTPUT_SPK_TYPE real ( wp ), public :: min_export_time_step = 0.0_wp !! minimum time (sec) step for exporting to mkspk file !! [to try and avoid spice interpolation issues for very small time steps] type , public :: patch_point !! a CR3BP Halo state, to be used as !! an initial guess for the full force model. real ( wp ) :: t = zero !! Time from Periapse (days from periapsis) real ( wp ), dimension ( 6 ) :: rv = zero !! Rx (km) !! Ry (km) !! Rz (km) !! Vx (km/s) !! Vy (km/s) !! Vz (km/s) [moon-centered earth-moon rotating frame] end type patch_point end module parameters_module","tags":"","url":"sourcefile/parameters_module.f90.html"},{"title":"halo_utilities_module.f90 – halo","text":"This file depends on sourcefile~~halo_utilities_module.f90~~EfferentGraph sourcefile~halo_utilities_module.f90 halo_utilities_module.f90 sourcefile~halo_kinds_module.f90 halo_kinds_module.F90 sourcefile~halo_utilities_module.f90->sourcefile~halo_kinds_module.f90 sourcefile~parameters_module.f90 parameters_module.f90 sourcefile~halo_utilities_module.f90->sourcefile~parameters_module.f90 sourcefile~splined_ephemeris_module.f90 splined_ephemeris_module.f90 sourcefile~halo_utilities_module.f90->sourcefile~splined_ephemeris_module.f90 sourcefile~parameters_module.f90->sourcefile~halo_kinds_module.f90 sourcefile~splined_ephemeris_module.f90->sourcefile~halo_kinds_module.f90 Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Source File Source File This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a file to a file which it depends on. A file\nis dependent upon another if the latter must be compiled before the former\ncan be. Files dependent on this one sourcefile~~halo_utilities_module.f90~~AfferentGraph sourcefile~halo_utilities_module.f90 halo_utilities_module.f90 sourcefile~halo_module.f90 halo_module.F90 sourcefile~halo_module.f90->sourcefile~halo_utilities_module.f90 sourcefile~halo_eclipse_opt_submodule.f90 halo_eclipse_opt_submodule.F90 sourcefile~halo_eclipse_opt_submodule.f90->sourcefile~halo_module.f90 Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Source File Source File This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a file to a file which it depends on. A file\nis dependent upon another if the latter must be compiled before the former\ncan be. Source Code !***************************************************************************************** !> !  Various astrodynamics utilities. ! !  The lighting routines it used to have (`apparent_position`, `cubic_shadow_model`, !  and the frame conversion to the solar system barycenter) are now in the Fortran !  Astrodynamics Toolkit's `lighting_module`. module halo_utilities_module ! (the toolkit's get_sun_fraction is more general [any eclipsing body, with the state !  relative to it]; the one here is for halo: Moon-centered state, eclipses by the Earth) use fortran_astrodynamics_toolkit , fat_get_sun_fraction => get_sun_fraction use iso_fortran_env use halo_kinds_module use splined_ephemeris_module use parameters_module implicit none private public :: get_sun_fraction contains !******************************************************************************** !******************************************************************************** !> !  Compute the \"sun fraction\" for eclipses by the Earth, using the circular !  cubic shadow model (the apparent positions of the Sun and the Earth). function get_sun_fraction ( eph , et , rv , rbubble ) result ( phi ) class ( jpl_ephemeris ), intent ( inout ) :: eph !! the ephemeris real ( wp ), dimension ( 6 ), intent ( in ) :: rv !! state of the spacecraft !! (j2000-moon frame) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: et !! observer ephemeris time (sec) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: rbubble !! eclipse bubble [km]. see the reference. real ( wp ) :: phi !! circular cubic sun frac value. !! !!  * >0 no eclipse, !!  * <0 eclipse, !!  * =0 on the eclipse line logical :: status_ok !! true if no problems real ( wp ), dimension ( 3 ) :: r_sun !! apparent state of the sun (j2000-ssb frame) real ( wp ), dimension ( 3 ) :: r_earth !! apparent state of the earth (j2000-ssb frame) real ( wp ), dimension ( 6 ) :: rv_ssb !! state of the spacecraft !! (j2000-ssb frame) call from_j2000body_to_j2000ssb ( body_moon , eph , et , rv , rv_ssb ) ! state of spacecraft in j2000-ssb call apparent_position ( eph , body_sun , et , rv_ssb , r_sun , status_ok ) ! apparent position of sun in j2000 call apparent_position ( eph , body_earth , et , rv_ssb , r_earth , status_ok ) ! apparent position of earth in j2000 call cubic_shadow_model ( r_sun , rad_sun , r_earth , rad_earth , phi , rbubble ) ! compute sun fraction value end function get_sun_fraction !******************************************************************************** end module halo_utilities_module","tags":"","url":"sourcefile/halo_utilities_module.f90.html"},{"title":"config_file_module.f90 – halo","text":"This file depends on sourcefile~~config_file_module.f90~~EfferentGraph sourcefile~config_file_module.f90 config_file_module.f90 sourcefile~parameters_module.f90 parameters_module.f90 sourcefile~config_file_module.f90->sourcefile~parameters_module.f90 sourcefile~halo_kinds_module.f90 halo_kinds_module.F90 sourcefile~parameters_module.f90->sourcefile~halo_kinds_module.f90 Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Source File Source File This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a file to a file which it depends on. A file\nis dependent upon another if the latter must be compiled before the former\ncan be. Files dependent on this one sourcefile~~config_file_module.f90~~AfferentGraph sourcefile~config_file_module.f90 config_file_module.f90 sourcefile~halo_module.f90 halo_module.F90 sourcefile~halo_module.f90->sourcefile~config_file_module.f90 sourcefile~halo_eclipse_opt_submodule.f90 halo_eclipse_opt_submodule.F90 sourcefile~halo_eclipse_opt_submodule.f90->sourcefile~halo_module.f90 Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Source File Source File This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a file to a file which it depends on. A file\nis dependent upon another if the latter must be compiled before the former\ncan be. Source Code !***************************************************************************************** !> !  For handling JSON config files module config_file_module use json_module , only : json_file use parameters_module , only : wp implicit none private type , public :: config_file !! a class for handling JSON config files. private character ( len = :), allocatable :: name !! the file name type ( json_file ), public :: json !! made it public so we can use the methods contains private procedure , public :: open => open_config_file procedure , public :: close => close_config_file generic , public :: get => get_int , get_real , get_logical , get_char ,& get_real_vec procedure , private :: get_int , get_real , get_logical , get_char , get_real_vec end type config_file contains !***************************************************************************************** !***************************************************************************************** !> !  Open the file. subroutine open_config_file ( me , filename ) class ( config_file ), intent ( inout ) :: me character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: filename !! the name of the JSON file call me % json % load ( filename = filename ) if ( me % json % failed ()) error stop 'error reading json file ' // trim ( filename ) end subroutine open_config_file !***************************************************************************************** !***************************************************************************************** !> !  Open the file. subroutine close_config_file ( me ) class ( config_file ), intent ( inout ) :: me call me % json % destroy () end subroutine close_config_file !***************************************************************************************** !********************************************** !> !  Get an integer variable from the config file. subroutine get_int ( me , name , variable , found ) class ( config_file ), intent ( inout ) :: me character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: name !! name of the variable integer , intent ( inout ) :: variable !! the variable to populate with the value logical , intent ( out ), optional :: found !! if the variable was in the file integer :: tmp logical :: required !! if the variable is required !! (if required and not found, `error stop` is called) logical :: was_found !! local copy of `found` required = . not . present ( found ) call me % json % get ( name , tmp , was_found ); if ( was_found ) variable = tmp if ( required . and . . not . was_found ) & error stop trim ( name ) // ' integer variable not found in config file: ' // trim ( me % name ) if ( present ( found )) found = was_found end subroutine get_int !********************************************** !********************************************** !> !  Get a real variable from the config file. subroutine get_real ( me , name , variable , found ) class ( config_file ), intent ( inout ) :: me character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: name !! name of the variable real ( wp ), intent ( inout ) :: variable !! the variable to populate with the value logical , intent ( out ), optional :: found !! if the variable was in the file real ( wp ) :: tmp logical :: required !! if the variable is required !! (if required and not found, `error stop` is called) logical :: was_found !! local copy of `found` required = . not . present ( found ) call me % json % get ( name , tmp , was_found ); if ( was_found ) variable = tmp if ( required . and . . not . was_found ) & error stop trim ( name ) // ' integer variable not found in config file: ' // trim ( me % name ) if ( present ( found )) found = was_found end subroutine get_real !********************************************** !********************************************** !> !  Get a logical variable from the config file. subroutine get_logical ( me , name , variable , found ) class ( config_file ), intent ( inout ) :: me character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: name !! name of the variable logical , intent ( inout ) :: variable !! the variable to populate with the value logical , intent ( out ), optional :: found !! if the variable was in the file logical :: tmp logical :: required !! if the variable is required !! (if required and not found, `error stop` is called) logical :: was_found !! local copy of `found` required = . not . present ( found ) call me % json % get ( name , tmp , was_found ); if ( was_found ) variable = tmp if ( required . and . . not . was_found ) & error stop trim ( name ) // ' integer variable not found in config file: ' // trim ( me % name ) if ( present ( found )) found = was_found end subroutine get_logical !********************************************** !********************************************** !> !  Get a character variable from the config file. subroutine get_char ( me , name , variable , found ) class ( config_file ), intent ( inout ) :: me character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: name !! name of the variable character ( len = :), allocatable , intent ( inout ) :: variable !! the variable to populate with the value logical , intent ( out ), optional :: found !! if the variable was in the file character ( len = :), allocatable :: tmp logical :: required !! if the variable is required !! (if required and not found, `error stop` is called) logical :: was_found !! local copy of `found` required = . not . present ( found ) call me % json % get ( name , tmp , was_found ); if ( was_found ) variable = tmp if ( required . and . . not . was_found ) & error stop trim ( name ) // ' integer variable not found in config file: ' // trim ( me % name ) if ( present ( found )) found = was_found end subroutine get_char !********************************************** !********************************************** !> !  Get a real vector from the config file. subroutine get_real_vec ( me , name , variable , found ) class ( config_file ), intent ( inout ) :: me character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: name !! name of the variable real ( wp ), dimension (:), allocatable , intent ( inout ) :: variable !! the variable to populate with the value logical , intent ( out ), optional :: found !! if the variable was in the file real ( wp ), dimension (:), allocatable :: tmp logical :: required !! if the variable is required !! (if required and not found, `error stop` is called) logical :: was_found !! local copy of `found` required = . not . present ( found ) call me % json % get ( name , tmp , was_found ); if ( was_found ) variable = tmp if ( required . and . . not . was_found ) & error stop trim ( name ) // ' integer variable not found in config file: ' // trim ( me % name ) if ( present ( found )) found = was_found end subroutine get_real_vec !********************************************** !***************************************************************************************** end module config_file_module !*****************************************************************************************","tags":"","url":"sourcefile/config_file_module.f90.html"},{"title":"halo_kinds_module.F90 – halo","text":"Files dependent on this one sourcefile~~halo_kinds_module.f90~~AfferentGraph sourcefile~halo_kinds_module.f90 halo_kinds_module.F90 sourcefile~astro_partials_module.f90 astro_partials_module.f90 sourcefile~astro_partials_module.f90->sourcefile~halo_kinds_module.f90 sourcefile~halo_utilities_module.f90 halo_utilities_module.f90 sourcefile~halo_utilities_module.f90->sourcefile~halo_kinds_module.f90 sourcefile~parameters_module.f90 parameters_module.f90 sourcefile~halo_utilities_module.f90->sourcefile~parameters_module.f90 sourcefile~splined_ephemeris_module.f90 splined_ephemeris_module.f90 sourcefile~halo_utilities_module.f90->sourcefile~splined_ephemeris_module.f90 sourcefile~parameters_module.f90->sourcefile~halo_kinds_module.f90 sourcefile~splined_ephemeris_module.f90->sourcefile~halo_kinds_module.f90 sourcefile~splined_moon_frame_module.f90 splined_moon_frame_module.f90 sourcefile~splined_moon_frame_module.f90->sourcefile~halo_kinds_module.f90 sourcefile~text_buffer_module.f90 text_buffer_module.f90 sourcefile~text_buffer_module.f90->sourcefile~halo_kinds_module.f90 sourcefile~config_file_module.f90 config_file_module.f90 sourcefile~config_file_module.f90->sourcefile~parameters_module.f90 sourcefile~halo_module.f90 halo_module.F90 sourcefile~halo_module.f90->sourcefile~astro_partials_module.f90 sourcefile~halo_module.f90->sourcefile~halo_utilities_module.f90 sourcefile~halo_module.f90->sourcefile~parameters_module.f90 sourcefile~halo_module.f90->sourcefile~splined_ephemeris_module.f90 sourcefile~halo_module.f90->sourcefile~splined_moon_frame_module.f90 sourcefile~halo_module.f90->sourcefile~text_buffer_module.f90 sourcefile~halo_module.f90->sourcefile~config_file_module.f90 sourcefile~halo_eclipse_opt_submodule.f90 halo_eclipse_opt_submodule.F90 sourcefile~halo_eclipse_opt_submodule.f90->sourcefile~halo_module.f90 Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Source File Source File This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a file to a file which it depends on. A file\nis dependent upon another if the latter must be compiled before the former\ncan be. Source Code !***************************************************************************************** !> !  Numeric kind definitions. module halo_kinds_module use , intrinsic :: iso_fortran_env implicit none private #ifdef REAL32 integer , parameter , public :: wp = real32 !! Real working precision [4 bytes] #elif REAL64 integer , parameter , public :: wp = real64 !! Real working precision [8 bytes] #elif REAL128 integer , parameter , public :: wp = real128 !! Real working precision [16 bytes] #else integer , parameter , public :: wp = real64 !! Real working precision if not specified [8 bytes] #endif ! #ifdef INT8 !     integer,parameter,public :: ip = int8     !! Integer working precision [1 byte] ! #elif INT16 !     integer,parameter,public :: ip = int16    !! Integer working precision [2 bytes] ! #elif INT32 !     integer,parameter,public :: ip = int32    !! Integer working precision [4 bytes] ! #elif INT64 !     integer,parameter,public :: ip = int64    !! Integer working precision [8 bytes] ! #else !     integer,parameter,public :: ip = int32    !! Integer working precision if not specified [4 bytes] ! #endif !***************************************************************************************** end module halo_kinds_module !*****************************************************************************************","tags":"","url":"sourcefile/halo_kinds_module.f90.html"},{"title":"splined_moon_frame_module.f90 – halo","text":"This file depends on sourcefile~~splined_moon_frame_module.f90~~EfferentGraph sourcefile~splined_moon_frame_module.f90 splined_moon_frame_module.f90 sourcefile~halo_kinds_module.f90 halo_kinds_module.F90 sourcefile~splined_moon_frame_module.f90->sourcefile~halo_kinds_module.f90 Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Source File Source File This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a file to a file which it depends on. A file\nis dependent upon another if the latter must be compiled before the former\ncan be. Files dependent on this one sourcefile~~splined_moon_frame_module.f90~~AfferentGraph sourcefile~splined_moon_frame_module.f90 splined_moon_frame_module.f90 sourcefile~halo_module.f90 halo_module.F90 sourcefile~halo_module.f90->sourcefile~splined_moon_frame_module.f90 sourcefile~halo_eclipse_opt_submodule.f90 halo_eclipse_opt_submodule.F90 sourcefile~halo_eclipse_opt_submodule.f90->sourcefile~halo_module.f90 Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Source File Source File This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a file to a file which it depends on. A file\nis dependent upon another if the latter must be compiled before the former\ncan be. Source Code !***************************************************************************************** !> !  Splined lunar principal-axis (MOON_PA) frame: the rotation from J2000 to the !  frame, interpolated from a table of the frame's roll, pitch and yaw angles vs. !  ephemeris time (e.g., `data/moon_pa_2000_2100.csv`, generated with SPICE). ! !  This is the same interpolation as the `moonframe` library's !  `moon_frame_interpolater` (quartic B-splines of the roll, the pitch, and the !  cosine and sine of the yaw angle, with the same knots), and gives identical !  results, but with the same pattern as [[splined_ephemeris_module]]: the spline !  coefficients are global variables, computed once and then only read, so all !  the segments (and threads) share one copy. Each [[moon_pa_frame]] object only !  holds its own small evaluation workspace (the interval indices and a work !  array, which `db1val` modifies), so each segment (thread) has its own. !  (With a copy of the coefficients in every segment, the memory grew with the !  square of the number of revolutions.) module splined_moon_frame_module use bspline_module , only : db1ink , db1val , bspline_order_quartic use csv_module , only : csv_file use halo_kinds_module implicit none private integer , parameter :: kx = bspline_order_quartic !! spline order (as in `moonframe`) integer , parameter :: iknot = 0 !! knots chosen by `db1ink` (as in `moonframe`) integer , parameter :: n_splines = 4 !! roll, pitch, cos(yaw), sin(yaw) ! the spline data: global variables, so there is only one copy ! (set by [[initialize_moon_pa_frame]], then only read): integer :: nx = 0 !! number of points real ( wp ), dimension (:,:), allocatable :: tx !! `(nx+kx, n_splines)` knots real ( wp ), dimension (:,:), allocatable :: bcoef !! `(nx, n_splines)` coefficients type , public :: moon_pa_frame !! The interface to the splined MOON_PA frame: only the evaluation workspace !! (the splines themselves are global). Make a copy for each thread. private integer , dimension ( n_splines ) :: inbvx = 1 !! `db1val`'s interval index for each spline real ( wp ), dimension ( 3 * kx ) :: w0 = 0.0_wp !! `db1val` work array contains private procedure , public :: initialize => initialize_moon_pa_frame procedure , public :: j2000_to_frame procedure , public :: frame_to_j2000 procedure , public :: destroy => destroy_moon_pa_frame end type moon_pa_frame contains !***************************************************************************************** !***************************************************************************************** !> !  Read the table and compute the (global) splines, for the time span `[et0, etf]`: !  the rows from the last one at or before `et0` to the first one at or after !  `etf` (as in `moonframe`). Then the object's workspace is reset; copies of !  the object (`allocate(..., source=...)`) can be used by other threads. subroutine initialize_moon_pa_frame ( me , filename , et0 , etf ) class ( moon_pa_frame ), intent ( inout ) :: me character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: filename !! csv file with the ephemeris time, roll, pitch and yaw (rad) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: et0 !! start ephemeris time of the span to spline [sec] real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: etf !! end ephemeris time of the span to spline [sec] type ( csv_file ) :: f real ( wp ), dimension (:), allocatable :: et , roll , pitch , yaw , fcn integer :: n , istart , iend , i , j , iflag logical :: status_ok ! read the data from the csv file: call f % read ( filename , header_row = 1 , status_ok = status_ok ) if (. not . status_ok ) error stop 'error reading file: ' // trim ( filename ) call f % get ( 1 , et , status_ok ); if (. not . status_ok ) error stop 'error getting et from file: ' // trim ( filename ) call f % get ( 2 , roll , status_ok ); if (. not . status_ok ) error stop 'error getting roll from file: ' // trim ( filename ) call f % get ( 3 , pitch , status_ok ); if (. not . status_ok ) error stop 'error getting pitch from file: ' // trim ( filename ) call f % get ( 4 , yaw , status_ok ); if (. not . status_ok ) error stop 'error getting yaw from file: ' // trim ( filename ) call f % destroy () ! the rows to use (the span, with the rows just outside it): n = size ( et ) istart = minloc ( abs ( et - et0 ), 1 ) if ( et ( istart ) > et0 ) istart = max ( 1 , istart - 1 ) iend = minloc ( abs ( et - etf ), 1 ) if ( et ( iend ) < etf ) iend = min ( n , iend + 1 ) if ( et ( iend ) < et ( istart )) error stop 'Error: end time is before start time' ! the global splines. roll and pitch have no discontinuities; the yaw angle wraps ! around once per lunar rotation, so its cosine and sine are splined instead. if ( allocated ( tx )) deallocate ( tx ) if ( allocated ( bcoef )) deallocate ( bcoef ) nx = iend - istart + 1 allocate ( tx ( nx + kx , n_splines ), bcoef ( nx , n_splines ), fcn ( nx )) do j = 1 , n_splines do i = istart , iend ! (a loop: no large temporaries on the stack) select case ( j ) case ( 1 ); fcn ( i - istart + 1 ) = roll ( i ) case ( 2 ); fcn ( i - istart + 1 ) = pitch ( i ) case ( 3 ); fcn ( i - istart + 1 ) = cos ( yaw ( i )) case ( 4 ); fcn ( i - istart + 1 ) = sin ( yaw ( i )) end select end do call db1ink ( et ( istart : iend ), nx , fcn , kx , iknot , tx (:, j ), bcoef (:, j ), iflag ) if ( iflag /= 0 ) error stop 'error initializing the MOON_PA spline: ' // trim ( filename ) end do call me % destroy () ! (reset the workspace) end subroutine initialize_moon_pa_frame !***************************************************************************************** !***************************************************************************************** !> !  The rotation matrix from J2000 to the MOON_PA frame at `et`. function j2000_to_frame ( me , et ) result ( rot ) class ( moon_pa_frame ), intent ( inout ) :: me real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: et !! ephemeris time [sec] real ( wp ), dimension ( 3 , 3 ) :: rot real ( wp ), dimension ( n_splines ) :: v !! roll, pitch, cos(yaw), sin(yaw) integer :: j , iflag if ( nx == 0 ) error stop 'error: the MOON_PA frame has not been initialized' do j = 1 , n_splines call db1val ( et , 0 , tx (:, j ), nx , kx , bcoef (:, j ), v ( j ), iflag , me % inbvx ( j ), me % w0 , extrap = . false .) if ( iflag /= 0 ) error stop 'error evaluating the MOON_PA spline.' end do call rpy_to_rot ( v ( 1 ), v ( 2 ), atan2 ( v ( 4 ), v ( 3 )), rot ) end function j2000_to_frame !***************************************************************************************** !***************************************************************************************** !> !  The rotation matrix from the MOON_PA frame to J2000 at `et`. function frame_to_j2000 ( me , et ) result ( rot ) class ( moon_pa_frame ), intent ( inout ) :: me real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: et !! ephemeris time [sec] real ( wp ), dimension ( 3 , 3 ) :: rot rot = transpose ( me % j2000_to_frame ( et )) end function frame_to_j2000 !***************************************************************************************** !***************************************************************************************** !> !  Roll, pitch and yaw (rad) to the rotation matrix (as in `moonframe`). pure subroutine rpy_to_rot ( roll , pitch , yaw , r ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: roll , pitch , yaw real ( wp ), dimension ( 3 , 3 ), intent ( out ) :: r real ( wp ) :: cr , sr , cp , sp , cy , sy cr = cos ( roll ) sr = sin ( roll ) cp = cos ( pitch ) sp = sin ( pitch ) cy = cos ( yaw ) sy = sin ( yaw ) r ( 1 , 1 ) = cy * cp r ( 1 , 2 ) = cy * sp * sr - sy * cr r ( 1 , 3 ) = cy * sp * cr + sy * sr r ( 2 , 1 ) = sy * cp r ( 2 , 2 ) = sy * sp * sr + cy * cr r ( 2 , 3 ) = sy * sp * cr - cy * sr r ( 3 , 1 ) = - sp r ( 3 , 2 ) = cp * sr r ( 3 , 3 ) = cp * cr end subroutine rpy_to_rot !***************************************************************************************** !***************************************************************************************** !> !  Reset the object's workspace (the global splines are kept). subroutine destroy_moon_pa_frame ( me ) class ( moon_pa_frame ), intent ( inout ) :: me me % inbvx = 1 me % w0 = 0.0_wp end subroutine destroy_moon_pa_frame !***************************************************************************************** end module splined_moon_frame_module !*****************************************************************************************","tags":"","url":"sourcefile/splined_moon_frame_module.f90.html"},{"title":"halo_module.F90 – halo","text":"This file depends on sourcefile~~halo_module.f90~~EfferentGraph sourcefile~halo_module.f90 halo_module.F90 sourcefile~astro_partials_module.f90 astro_partials_module.f90 sourcefile~halo_module.f90->sourcefile~astro_partials_module.f90 sourcefile~config_file_module.f90 config_file_module.f90 sourcefile~halo_module.f90->sourcefile~config_file_module.f90 sourcefile~halo_utilities_module.f90 halo_utilities_module.f90 sourcefile~halo_module.f90->sourcefile~halo_utilities_module.f90 sourcefile~parameters_module.